<span class="ltx_bibblock"><em id="bib.bib35.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Advances in Neural Information Processing Systems</em>, 35:36958–36971, 2022.

</span></li>
      
<li id="bib.bib36" class="ltx_bibitem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_role_refnum ltx_tag_bibitem">Zhang et al. (2023a)</span>
<span class="ltx_bibblock">
R. Zhang, S. Frei, and P. L. Bartlett.

</span>
<span class="ltx_bibblock">Trained transformers learn linear models in-context.

</span>
<span class="ltx_bibblock"><em id="bib.bib36.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">arXiv preprint arXiv:2306.09927</em>, 2023a.

</span></li>
      
<li id="bib.bib37" class="ltx_bibitem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_role_refnum ltx_tag_bibitem">Zhang et al. (2023b)</span>
<span class="ltx_bibblock">
Y. Zhang, F. Zhang, Z. Yang, and Z. Wang.

</span>
<span class="ltx_bibblock">What and how does in-context learning learn? bayesian model averaging, parameterization, and generalization.

</span>
<span class="ltx_bibblock"><em id="bib.bib37.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">arXiv preprint arXiv:2305.19420</em>, 2023b.

</span></li>
    
</ul>
</section>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Justification of modeling and assumptions</h2>

<div id="Thmrmk9" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_rmk">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmrmk9.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Remark 9</span></span><span id="Thmrmk9.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmrmk9.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmrmk9.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmrmk9.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The above modeling of sequence generation effectively captures key characteristics of natural language generation, ensuring both coherence and factual alignment. 1) Topic Consistency: Usually <math id="Thmrmk9.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p_{t}(\cdot|\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{t}(\cdot|\theta)</annotation></semantics></math> assigns higher probability to topics related to <math id="Thmrmk9.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math>; 2) The class attributes of key tokens align with real-world facts, as determined by the first token. In addition, it is important to highlight that unrelated topics—such as ‘Occupation’ and ‘Geography’—are unlikely to occur under a shared concept. Even if two words belong to the same class (e.g, ‘Trump’ and ‘Earthquake’), they are not likely to appear together in the same sequence.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmrmk10" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_rmk">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmrmk10.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Remark 10</span></span><span id="Thmrmk10.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmrmk10.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmrmk10.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmrmk10.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">(Justifying Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption1" title="Assumption 1. ‣ 2.3 Comparing proposed context construction with existing works ‣ 2 The Proposed Framework of Modeling Data Generation and Prediction ‣ A Framework for Quantifying How Pre-Training and Context Benefit In-Context Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>)
In Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption1" title="Assumption 1. ‣ 2.3 Comparing proposed context construction with existing works ‣ 2 The Proposed Framework of Modeling Data Generation and Prediction ‣ A Framework for Quantifying How Pre-Training and Context Benefit In-Context Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, we make two relatively strong assumptions, i.e (i) and (ii). We clarify that (i) and (ii) are reasonable in our illustrated example to show the difference in the predictions with (<a href="#S2.E2" title="In 2.2 Modeling ICL prediction with pre-trained LM ‣ 2 The Proposed Framework of Modeling Data Generation and Prediction ‣ A Framework for Quantifying How Pre-Training and Context Benefit In-Context Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>) and (<a href="#S2.EGx3" title="2.3 Comparing proposed context construction with existing works ‣ 2 The Proposed Framework of Modeling Data Generation and Prediction ‣ A Framework for Quantifying How Pre-Training and Context Benefit In-Context Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.3</span></a>). (i) is commonly used in literature <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">Huang et al., 2023</a>, <a href="#bib.bib36" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhang et al., 2023a</a>]</cite>, where the masked output is denoted as <math id="Thmrmk10.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>𝟎</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{0}</annotation></semantics></math> (which is showed in (<a href="#S2.EGx3" title="2.3 Comparing proposed context construction with existing works ‣ 2 The Proposed Framework of Modeling Data Generation and Prediction ‣ A Framework for Quantifying How Pre-Training and Context Benefit In-Context Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.3</span></a>)). (ii) assumes uniform attention. However, notice that for general <math id="Thmrmk10.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{W}^{Q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>Q</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{W}^{Q}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmrmk10.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{W}^{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>K</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{W}^{K}</annotation></semantics></math>, it only changes the coefficient of the embedded context samples and <math id="Thmrmk10.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{\text{q}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">q</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{\text{q}}</annotation></semantics></math> in (<a href="#S2.E6" title="In 2.3 Comparing proposed context construction with existing works ‣ 2 The Proposed Framework of Modeling Data Generation and Prediction ‣ A Framework for Quantifying How Pre-Training and Context Benefit In-Context Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>), and the coefficient of <math id="Thmrmk10.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> in (<a href="#S2.E7" title="In 2.3 Comparing proposed context construction with existing works ‣ 2 The Proposed Framework of Modeling Data Generation and Prediction ‣ A Framework for Quantifying How Pre-Training and Context Benefit In-Context Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>). More specifically, for the term <math id="Thmrmk10.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{W}^{V}(X_{i}+y_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>V</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{W}^{V}(X_{i}+y_{i})</annotation></semantics></math> in (<a href="#S2.E6" title="In 2.3 Comparing proposed context construction with existing works ‣ 2 The Proposed Framework of Modeling Data Generation and Prediction ‣ A Framework for Quantifying How Pre-Training and Context Benefit In-Context Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>), the coefficient is some constant rather than <math id="Thmrmk10.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{2n+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{2n+1}</annotation></semantics></math>; in (<a href="#S2.E7" title="In 2.3 Comparing proposed context construction with existing works ‣ 2 The Proposed Framework of Modeling Data Generation and Prediction ‣ A Framework for Quantifying How Pre-Training and Context Benefit In-Context Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>), the coefficients of <math id="Thmrmk10.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is some constant instead of <math id="Thmrmk10.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{n+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{n+1}</annotation></semantics></math>. This does not change the fundamental difference between (<a href="#S2.E6" title="In 2.3 Comparing proposed context construction with existing works ‣ 2 The Proposed Framework of Modeling Data Generation and Prediction ‣ A Framework for Quantifying How Pre-Training and Context Benefit In-Context Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>) and (<a href="#S2.E7" title="In 2.3 Comparing proposed context construction with existing works ‣ 2 The Proposed Framework of Modeling Data Generation and Prediction ‣ A Framework for Quantifying How Pre-Training and Context Benefit In-Context Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>).</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmrmk11" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_rmk">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmrmk11.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Remark 11</span></span><span id="Thmrmk11.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmrmk11.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmrmk11.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmrmk11.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption2" title="Assumption 2. ‣ 3.3 Pre-trained One-layer Transformer ‣ 3 A Statistical Model: Pre-trained Transformer Shifts the Output Distribution ‣ A Framework for Quantifying How Pre-Training and Context Benefit In-Context Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> characterizes the correlation (quantified by attention <math id="Thmrmk11.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math>) between the masked words <math id="Thmrmk11.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="({(\widetilde{X}_{\text{q}})}_{:,j},\;L_{1}+1\leqslant j\leqslant N)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">q</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>⩽</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>⩽</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({(\widetilde{X}_{\text{q}})}_{:,j},\;L_{1}+1\leqslant j\leqslant N)</annotation></semantics></math> and the previous words with the attention head. Intuitively, when a word is far from the masked word in a sequence, it contributes less to the masked word in prediction. We model this position factor by an ascending sequence of weights <math id="Thmrmk11.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{1}&lt;a_{2}&lt;\cdots&lt;a_{n+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">&lt;</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.1389em">⋯</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em">&lt;</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{1}&lt;a_{2}&lt;\cdots&lt;a_{n+1}</annotation></semantics></math>. For a sequence with a length larger than <math id="Thmrmk11.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math>, we assume the correlation between the word and the masked word will decay with the “distance” increasing (thus <math id="Thmrmk11.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{i}&lt;a_{i}^{\prime},\forall i&lt;i^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{i}&lt;a_{i}^{\prime},\forall i&lt;i^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>). To simplify our analysis, we assume the token correlation within length <math id="Thmrmk11.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> be a uniform matrix (with each entry in <math id="Thmrmk11.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> equal to <math id="Thmrmk11.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{N}</annotation></semantics></math>). In Appendix <a href="#A4" title="Appendix D Experiment Details for Synthetic Data ‣ A Framework for Quantifying How Pre-Training and Context Benefit In-Context Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D</span></a>, we empirically verify that if we freeze uniform attention and only update <math id="Thmrmk11.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{W}^{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>V</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{W}^{V}</annotation></semantics></math> in the training phase, the performance is very close to updating all the variables. A similar observation is found in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib19" title="" class="ltx_ref">Li et al., 2023b</a>]</cite>, where most theoretical results are also based on uniform attention.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<figure id="A1.F5" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2510.22594v1/../figure/tableexample.png" id="A1.F5.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:381/157;" width="381" height="157" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A1.F5.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 5</span>: </span><span id="A1.F5.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Example of encoded sequence.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Proof of Theorem <a href="#Thmthm1" title="Theorem 1. ‣ 4 Generalized Case: Quantify the effect of Context in ICL ‣ A Framework for Quantifying How Pre-Training and Context Benefit In-Context Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a></h2>

<div id="A2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">We can derive the prediction probability of label <math id="A2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math> as:</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx19" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\quad p\left(y\mid R_{1},R_{2},\cdots,R_{H},S_{n},X_{\text{q}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mtext>q</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad p\left(y\mid R_{1},R_{2},\cdots,R_{H},S_{n},X_{\text{q}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\int_{\theta}p\left(y\mid R_{1},R_{2},\cdots,R_{H},S_{n},X_{\text{q}},\theta\right)p\left(\theta\mid R_{1},R_{2},\cdots,R_{H},S_{n},X_{\text{q}}\right)d\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mtext>q</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mtext>q</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int_{\theta}p\left(y\mid R_{1},R_{2},\cdots,R_{H},S_{n},X_{\text{q}},\theta\right)p\left(\theta\mid R_{1},R_{2},\cdots,R_{H},S_{n},X_{\text{q}}\right)d\theta</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\propto\int_{\theta}p\left(y\mid R_{1},R_{2},\cdots,R_{H},S_{n},X_{\text{q}},\theta\right)p\left(R_{1},R_{2},\cdots,R_{H},S_{n},X_{\text{q}}\mid\theta\right)p(\theta)d\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>∝</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mtext>q</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mtext>q</mtext></msub></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\propto\int_{\theta}p\left(y\mid R_{1},R_{2},\cdots,R_{H},S_{n},X_{\text{q}},\theta\right)p\left(R_{1},R_{2},\cdots,R_{H},S_{n},X_{\text{q}}\mid\theta\right)p(\theta)d\theta</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\propto\int_{\theta}p\left(y\mid S_{n},X_{\text{q}},\theta\right)\cdot\frac{p\left(R_{1},R_{2},\cdots,R_{H},S_{n},X_{\text{q}}\mid\theta\right)}{p\left(R_{1},R_{2},\cdots,R_{H},S_{n},X_{\text{q}}\mid\theta^{*}\right)}\cdot p\left(\theta\right)d\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>∝</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mtext>q</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mtext>q</mtext></msub></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mtext>q</mtext></msub></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\propto\int_{\theta}p\left(y\mid S_{n},X_{\text{q}},\theta\right)\cdot\frac{p\left(R_{1},R_{2},\cdots,R_{H},S_{n},X_{\text{q}}\mid\theta\right)}{p\left(R_{1},R_{2},\cdots,R_{H},S_{n},X_{\text{q}}\mid\theta^{*}\right)}\cdot p\left(\theta\right)d\theta</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\propto\int_{\theta}p\left(y\mid S_{n},X_{\text{q}},\theta\right)\cdot\frac{p\left(R_{1},R_{2},\cdots,R_{H}\mid\theta\right)}{p\left(R_{1},R_{2},\cdots,R_{h}\mid\theta^{*}\right)}\cdot\frac{p\left(S_{n},X_{\text{q}}\mid\theta\right)}{p\left(S_{n},X_{\text{q}}\mid\theta^{*}\right)}\cdot p\left(\theta\right)d\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>∝</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mtext>q</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>H</mi></msub></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mtext>q</mtext></msub></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mtext>q</mtext></msub></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\propto\int_{\theta}p\left(y\mid S_{n},X_{\text{q}},\theta\right)\cdot\frac{p\left(R_{1},R_{2},\cdots,R_{H}\mid\theta\right)}{p\left(R_{1},R_{2},\cdots,R_{h}\mid\theta^{*}\right)}\cdot\frac{p\left(S_{n},X_{\text{q}}\mid\theta\right)}{p\left(S_{n},X_{\text{q}}\mid\theta^{*}\right)}\cdot p\left(\theta\right)d\theta</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text">Next, we aim to show that</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx20" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex17"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{p\left(R_{1},R_{2},\cdots,R_{H}\mid\theta\right)}{p\left(R_{1},R_{2},\cdots,R_{H}\mid\theta^{*}\right)}\cdot\frac{p\left(S_{n},X_{\text{q}}\mid\theta\right)}{p\left(S_{n},X_{\text{q}}\mid\theta^{*}\right)}\stackrel{{\scriptstyle n\rightarrow\infty}}{{\longrightarrow}}0,\;\forall\theta\neq\theta^{*}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>H</mi></msub></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>H</mi></msub></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mtext>q</mtext></msub></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mtext>q</mtext></msub></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mover><mo stretchy="false">⟶</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mover><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo>≠</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{p\left(R_{1},R_{2},\cdots,R_{H}\mid\theta\right)}{p\left(R_{1},R_{2},\cdots,R_{H}\mid\theta^{*}\right)}\cdot\frac{p\left(S_{n},X_{\text{q}}\mid\theta\right)}{p\left(S_{n},X_{\text{q}}\mid\theta^{*}\right)}\stackrel{{\scriptstyle n\rightarrow\infty}}{{\longrightarrow}}0,\;\forall\theta\neq\theta^{*}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text">Define <math id="A2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{n_{1}}(\theta):=\frac{1}{n_{1}H}\sum\limits_{h=1}^{H}\sum\limits_{i=1}^{n_{1}}\log\frac{p\left(R_{h,i}\mid\theta\right)}{p\left(R_{h,i}\mid\theta^{*}\right)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>H</mi></munderover><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></munderover><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{n_{1}}(\theta):=\frac{1}{n_{1}H}\sum\limits_{h=1}^{H}\sum\limits_{i=1}^{n_{1}}\log\frac{p\left(R_{h,i}\mid\theta\right)}{p\left(R_{h,i}\mid\theta^{*}\right)}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{n}(\theta):=\frac{1}{n}\sum\limits_{i=1}^{n}\log\frac{p\left(s_{i}\mid\theta\right)}{p\left(s_{i}\mid\theta^{*}\right)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{n}(\theta):=\frac{1}{n}\sum\limits_{i=1}^{n}\log\frac{p\left(s_{i}\mid\theta\right)}{p\left(s_{i}\mid\theta^{*}\right)}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then we have</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx21" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex18"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{p\left(R_{1},R_{2},\cdots,R_{H}\mid\theta\right)}{p\left(R_{1},R_{2},\cdots,R_{H}\mid\theta^{*}\right)}\cdot\frac{p\left(S_{n},X_{\text{q}}\mid\theta\right)}{p\left(S_{n},X_{\text{q}}\mid\theta^{*}\right)}=\exp\left(n_{1}H\cdot r_{n_{1}}(\theta)+n\cdot q_{n}(\theta)\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>H</mi></msub></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>H</mi></msub></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mtext>q</mtext></msub></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mtext>q</mtext></msub></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{p\left(R_{1},R_{2},\cdots,R_{H}\mid\theta\right)}{p\left(R_{1},R_{2},\cdots,R_{H}\mid\theta^{*}\right)}\cdot\frac{p\left(S_{n},X_{\text{q}}\mid\theta\right)}{p\left(S_{n},X_{\text{q}}\mid\theta^{*}\right)}=\exp\left(n_{1}H\cdot r_{n_{1}}(\theta)+n\cdot q_{n}(\theta)\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text">(1) With probability<math id="A2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="&gt;0.999" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0.999</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">&gt;0.999</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{n_{1}}(\theta)&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{n_{1}}(\theta)&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math>.
We know <math id="A2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\forall i\in[n_{1}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\forall i\in[n_{1}]</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx22" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[r_{n_{1}}(\theta)]=\mathbb{E}_{R_{h,i}\sim p(\cdot\mid\theta_{h})}\left[\frac{1}{n_{1}T}\sum_{h=1}^{H}\sum_{i=1}^{n_{1}}\log\frac{p\left(R_{h,i}\mid\theta\right)}{p\left(R_{h,i}\mid\theta^{*}\right)}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>R</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>θ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>H</mi></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></munderover></mstyle><mi>log</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[r_{n_{1}}(\theta)]=\mathbb{E}_{R_{h,i}\sim p(\cdot\mid\theta_{h})}\left[\frac{1}{n_{1}T}\sum_{h=1}^{H}\sum_{i=1}^{n_{1}}\log\frac{p\left(R_{h,i}\mid\theta\right)}{p\left(R_{h,i}\mid\theta^{*}\right)}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex20"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{H}\sum_{h=1}^{H}\mathbb{E}_{R_{h,i}\sim p(\cdot\mid\theta_{h})}\left[\log\frac{p\left(R_{h,i}\mid\theta\right)}{p\left(R_{h,i}\mid\theta^{*}\right)}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>H</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>H</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>R</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>θ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>log</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{H}\sum_{h=1}^{H}\mathbb{E}_{R_{h,i}\sim p(\cdot\mid\theta_{h})}\left[\log\frac{p\left(R_{h,i}\mid\theta\right)}{p\left(R_{h,i}\mid\theta^{*}\right)}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{T}\sum_{h=1}^{H}\mathbb{E}_{R_{h,i}\sim p(\cdot\mid\theta_{h})}\left[\log\frac{p\left(R_{h,i}\mid\theta\right)}{p\left(R_{h,i}\mid\theta_{h}\right)}+\log\frac{p\left(R_{h,i}\mid\theta_{h}\right)}{p\left(R_{h,i}\mid\theta^{*}\right)}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>H</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>R</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>θ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>log</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mi>log</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{T}\sum_{h=1}^{H}\mathbb{E}_{R_{h,i}\sim p(\cdot\mid\theta_{h})}\left[\log\frac{p\left(R_{h,i}\mid\theta\right)}{p\left(R_{h,i}\mid\theta_{h}\right)}+\log\frac{p\left(R_{h,i}\mid\theta_{h}\right)}{p\left(R_{h,i}\mid\theta^{*}\right)}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex22"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{T}\sum\limits_{t=1}^{T}\text{KL}\left(p\left(\cdot\mid\theta_{h}\right)||p\left(\cdot\mid\theta^{*}\right)\right)-\text{KL}\left(p\left(\cdot\mid\theta_{h}\right)||p\left(\cdot\mid\theta\right)\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover></mstyle><mtext>KL</mtext><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mtext>KL</mtext><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{T}\sum\limits_{t=1}^{T}\text{KL}\left(p\left(\cdot\mid\theta_{h}\right)||p\left(\cdot\mid\theta^{*}\right)\right)-\text{KL}\left(p\left(\cdot\mid\theta_{h}\right)||p\left(\cdot\mid\theta\right)\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p1.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p1.5.1" class="ltx_text">By Assumption, we have</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx23" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{1}{T}\sum_{h=1}^{H}\mathrm{KL}\left(p\left(\cdot\mid\theta_{h}^{*}\right)\|p\left(\cdot\mid\theta^{*}\right)\right)-\operatorname{KL}\left(p\left(\cdot\mid\theta_{h}\right)\|p(\cdot\mid\theta)\right):=c_{1}&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>H</mi></munderover></mstyle><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>h</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>:=</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{1}{T}\sum_{h=1}^{H}\mathrm{KL}\left(p\left(\cdot\mid\theta_{h}^{*}\right)\|p\left(\cdot\mid\theta^{*}\right)\right)-\operatorname{KL}\left(p\left(\cdot\mid\theta_{h}\right)\|p(\cdot\mid\theta)\right):=c_{1}&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p1.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p1.6.1" class="ltx_text">In addition, By Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption7" title="Assumption 7. ‣ 4 Generalized Case: Quantify the effect of Context in ICL ‣ A Framework for Quantifying How Pre-Training and Context Benefit In-Context Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>, the variance of <math id="A2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{n_{1}}(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{n_{1}}(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math> can be bounded as following:</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx24" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex24"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\operatorname{var}\left(r_{n_{1}}(\theta)\right)=\operatorname{var}\left(\frac{1}{n_{1}T}\sum_{h=1}^{H}\sum_{i=1}^{n_{1}}\log\frac{p\left(R_{h,i}\mid\theta\right)}{p\left(R_{h,i}\mid\theta^{*}\right)}\right)\leqslant\frac{\sigma^{2}}{n_{1}H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>H</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\operatorname{var}\left(r_{n_{1}}(\theta)\right)=\operatorname{var}\left(\frac{1}{n_{1}T}\sum_{h=1}^{H}\sum_{i=1}^{n_{1}}\log\frac{p\left(R_{h,i}\mid\theta\right)}{p\left(R_{h,i}\mid\theta^{*}\right)}\right)\leqslant\frac{\sigma^{2}}{n_{1}H}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p1.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p1.7.1" class="ltx_text">Then by Central Limit Theorem (CLT), with probability <math id="A2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="&gt;0.999" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0.999</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">&gt;0.999</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx25" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex25"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle r_{n_{1}}(\theta)&lt;c_{1}+\frac{3\sigma}{\sqrt{n_{1}H}}:=c_{1}^{\prime}&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow><msqrt><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>:=</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle r_{n_{1}}(\theta)&lt;c_{1}+\frac{3\sigma}{\sqrt{n_{1}H}}:=c_{1}^{\prime}&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">(2) With probability <math id="A2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="&gt;0.999" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0.999</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">&gt;0.999</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{n}(\theta)&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{n}(\theta)&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. Similar to the derivation in (1), we have</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx26" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex26"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle q_{n}(\theta)\leqslant-KL\left(p\left(\cdot\mid\theta^{*}\right)||p\left(\cdot\mid\theta\right)\right)+\frac{3\sigma}{\sqrt{n}}:=c_{2}^{\prime}&lt;0." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">⩽</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>K</mi><mi>L</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow><msqrt><mi>n</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo>:=</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle q_{n}(\theta)\leqslant-KL\left(p\left(\cdot\mid\theta^{*}\right)||p\left(\cdot\mid\theta\right)\right)+\frac{3\sigma}{\sqrt{n}}:=c_{2}^{\prime}&lt;0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="A2.EGx27" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex27"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{p\left(R_{1},R_{2},\cdots,R_{H}\mid\theta\right)}{p\left(R_{1},R_{2},\cdots,R_{H}\mid\theta^{*}\right)}\cdot\frac{p\left(S_{n},X_{\text{q}}\mid\theta\right)}{p\left(S_{n},X_{\text{q}}\mid\theta^{*}\right)}=\exp\left(n_{1}H\cdot r_{n_{1}}(\theta)+n\cdot q_{n}(\theta)\right)&lt;\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>H</mi></msub></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>H</mi></msub></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mtext>q</mtext></msub></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mtext>q</mtext></msub></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{p\left(R_{1},R_{2},\cdots,R_{H}\mid\theta\right)}{p\left(R_{1},R_{2},\cdots,R_{H}\mid\theta^{*}\right)}\cdot\frac{p\left(S_{n},X_{\text{q}}\mid\theta\right)}{p\left(S_{n},X_{\text{q}}\mid\theta^{*}\right)}=\exp\left(n_{1}H\cdot r_{n_{1}}(\theta)+n\cdot q_{n}(\theta)\right)&lt;\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">Then we can derive</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx28" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex28"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle-(n_{1}Hc_{1}^{\prime}+nc_{2}^{\prime})&gt;\log\frac{1}{\epsilon}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>ϵ</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-(n_{1}Hc_{1}^{\prime}+nc_{2}^{\prime})&gt;\log\frac{1}{\epsilon}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">Suppose holds, then we have the following equation:</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx29" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex29"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\int_{\theta}p\left(y\mid S_{n},X_{\text{q}},\theta\right)\cdot\frac{p\left(R_{1},R_{2},\cdots,R_{H}\mid\theta\right)}{p\left(R_{1},R_{2},\cdots,R_{H}\mid\theta^{*}\right)}\cdot\frac{p\left(S_{n},X_{\text{q}}\mid\theta\right)}{p\left(S_{n},X_{\text{q}}\mid\theta^{*}\right)}\cdot p(\theta)d\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mtext>q</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>H</mi></msub></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>H</mi></msub></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mtext>q</mtext></msub></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mtext>q</mtext></msub></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\int_{\theta}p\left(y\mid S_{n},X_{\text{q}},\theta\right)\cdot\frac{p\left(R_{1},R_{2},\cdots,R_{H}\mid\theta\right)}{p\left(R_{1},R_{2},\cdots,R_{H}\mid\theta^{*}\right)}\cdot\frac{p\left(S_{n},X_{\text{q}}\mid\theta\right)}{p\left(S_{n},X_{\text{q}}\mid\theta^{*}\right)}\cdot p(\theta)d\theta</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex30"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=p\left(y\mid S_{n},X_{\text{q}},\theta^{*}\right)p\left(\theta^{*}\right)+\int_{\theta\neq\theta^{*}}p\left(y\mid S_{n},X_{\text{q}},\theta\right)\cdot\exp\left(n_{1}H\cdot r_{n_{1}}(\theta)+n\cdot q_{n}(\theta)\right)\cdot p(\theta)d\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mtext>q</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>≠</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mtext>q</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=p\left(y\mid S_{n},X_{\text{q}},\theta^{*}\right)p\left(\theta^{*}\right)+\int_{\theta\neq\theta^{*}}p\left(y\mid S_{n},X_{\text{q}},\theta\right)\cdot\exp\left(n_{1}H\cdot r_{n_{1}}(\theta)+n\cdot q_{n}(\theta)\right)\cdot p(\theta)d\theta</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex31"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\propto p\left(y\mid S_{n},X_{\text{q}},\theta^{*}\right)+\frac{1}{p(\theta^{*})}\int_{\theta\neq\theta^{*}}p\left(y\mid S_{n},X_{\text{q}},\theta\right)\cdot\exp\left(n_{1}H\cdot r_{n_{1}}(\theta)+n\cdot q_{n}(\theta)\right)\cdot p(\theta)d\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>∝</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mtext>q</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>≠</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mtext>q</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\propto p\left(y\mid S_{n},X_{\text{q}},\theta^{*}\right)+\frac{1}{p(\theta^{*})}\int_{\theta\neq\theta^{*}}p\left(y\mid S_{n},X_{\text{q}},\theta\right)\cdot\exp\left(n_{1}H\cdot r_{n_{1}}(\theta)+n\cdot q_{n}(\theta)\right)\cdot p(\theta)d\theta</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex32"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=p\left(y\mid S_{n},X_{\text{q}},\theta^{*}\right)+\frac{1}{p(\theta^{*})}\int_{\theta\neq\theta^{*}}\epsilon_{\theta}(y)\cdot p(\theta)d\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mtext>q</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>≠</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=p\left(y\mid S_{n},X_{\text{q}},\theta^{*}\right)+\frac{1}{p(\theta^{*})}\int_{\theta\neq\theta^{*}}\epsilon_{\theta}(y)\cdot p(\theta)d\theta</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p2.4.1" class="ltx_text">Thus, we can conclude that</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx30" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex33"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle p\left(y\mid R_{1},R_{2},\cdots,R_{h},S_{n},X_{\text{q}}\right)\propto p\left(y\mid S_{n},X_{\text{q}},\theta^{*}\right)+\frac{1}{p\left(\theta^{*}\right)}\int_{\theta\neq\theta^{*}}\epsilon_{\theta}(y)\cdot p(\theta)d\theta,\;\forall y." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mtext>q</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∝</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mtext>q</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>≠</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p\left(y\mid R_{1},R_{2},\cdots,R_{h},S_{n},X_{\text{q}}\right)\propto p\left(y\mid S_{n},X_{\text{q}},\theta^{*}\right)+\frac{1}{p\left(\theta^{*}\right)}\int_{\theta\neq\theta^{*}}\epsilon_{\theta}(y)\cdot p(\theta)d\theta,\;\forall y.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p2.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p2.5.1" class="ltx_text">Since we know</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx31" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex34"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle c\sum\limits_{y\in\mathcal{Y}}p\left(y\mid S_{n},X_{\text{q}},\theta^{*}\right)+\frac{1}{p\left(\theta^{*}\right)}\int_{\theta\neq\theta^{*}}\epsilon_{\theta}(y)\cdot p(\theta)d\theta=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mtext>q</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>≠</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle c\sum\limits_{y\in\mathcal{Y}}p\left(y\mid S_{n},X_{\text{q}},\theta^{*}\right)+\frac{1}{p\left(\theta^{*}\right)}\int_{\theta\neq\theta^{*}}\epsilon_{\theta}(y)\cdot p(\theta)d\theta=1</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p2.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p2.6.1" class="ltx_text">We have <math id="A2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c=1/\sum_{y\in\mathcal{Y}}p\left(y\mid S_{n},X_{\text{q}},\theta^{*}\right)+\frac{1}{p\left(\theta^{*}\right)}\int_{\theta\neq\boldsymbol{\theta}^{*}}\epsilon_{\theta}(y)\cdot p(\theta)d\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo rspace="0.055em">/</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mtext>q</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>≠</mo><msup><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c=1/\sum_{y\in\mathcal{Y}}p\left(y\mid S_{n},X_{\text{q}},\theta^{*}\right)+\frac{1}{p\left(\theta^{*}\right)}\int_{\theta\neq\boldsymbol{\theta}^{*}}\epsilon_{\theta}(y)\cdot p(\theta)d\theta</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y^{*}=\operatorname{argmax}_{y\in\mathcal{Y}}p\left(y\mid S_{n},X_{\text{q}},\theta\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>argmax</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mtext>q</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y^{*}=\operatorname{argmax}_{y\in\mathcal{Y}}p\left(y\mid S_{n},X_{\text{q}},\theta\right)</annotation></semantics></math></span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx32" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex35"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle p\left(y^{*}\mid R_{1},R_{2},\cdots,R_{H},S_{n},X_{\text{q}}\right)=c\cdot p\left(y^{*}\mid S_{n},X_{\text{q}},\theta^{*}\right)+\frac{1}{p\left(\theta^{*}\right)}\int_{\theta\neq\boldsymbol{\theta}^{*}}\epsilon_{\theta}(y)\cdot p(\theta)d\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mtext>q</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mtext>q</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>≠</mo><msup><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p\left(y^{*}\mid R_{1},R_{2},\cdots,R_{H},S_{n},X_{\text{q}}\right)=c\cdot p\left(y^{*}\mid S_{n},X_{\text{q}},\theta^{*}\right)+\frac{1}{p\left(\theta^{*}\right)}\int_{\theta\neq\boldsymbol{\theta}^{*}}\epsilon_{\theta}(y)\cdot p(\theta)d\theta</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex36"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geqslant c\cdot p\left(y^{*}\mid S_{n},X_{\text{q}},\theta^{*}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⩾</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mtext>q</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geqslant c\cdot p\left(y^{*}\mid S_{n},X_{\text{q}},\theta^{*}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex37"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle&gt;c\cdot\left(\max\limits_{y\neq y^{*}}p\left(y\mid S_{n},X_{\text{q}},\theta^{*}\right)+\frac{\epsilon}{p(\theta^{*})}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>≠</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mtext>q</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle&gt;c\cdot\left(\max\limits_{y\neq y^{*}}p\left(y\mid S_{n},X_{\text{q}},\theta^{*}\right)+\frac{\epsilon}{p(\theta^{*})}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p2.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p2.7.1" class="ltx_text">Thus, we can conclude that <math id="A2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{argmax}_{y\in\mathcal{Y}}p\left(y\mid R_{1},R_{2},\cdots,R_{H},S_{n},X_{\text{q}}\right)=y^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>argmax</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mtext>q</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{argmax}_{y\in\mathcal{Y}}p\left(y\mid R_{1},R_{2},\cdots,R_{H},S_{n},X_{\text{q}}\right)=y^{*}</annotation></semantics></math></span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Proof of Claim <a href="#Thmclaim1" title="Claim 1. ‣ 3.3 Pre-trained One-layer Transformer ‣ 3 A Statistical Model: Pre-trained Transformer Shifts the Output Distribution ‣ A Framework for Quantifying How Pre-Training and Context Benefit In-Context Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a></h2>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">(1) <span id="A3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Prediction without ICL:</span> This is computed directly by</p>
<table id="A3.Ex38" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex38.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\widehat{y}_{\text{q}}=f_{\bf w}(\widetilde{U}_{\text{q}})_{1:D,L_{1}+1:N}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mtext>q</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝐰</mi></msub><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>U</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mtext>q</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{y}_{\text{q}}=f_{\bf w}(\widetilde{U}_{\text{q}})_{1:D,L_{1}+1:N}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">(2) <span id="A3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Prediction with ICL:</span> Given additional <math id="A3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> encoded context samples <math id="A3.p2.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="S_{n}=s_{1:n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>s</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{n}=s_{1:n}</annotation></semantics></math>, with encoded matrix <math id="A3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{i}\in{\{0,1\}^{(T+K+2)\times N}}\sim\mathcal{D}_{\text{q}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msup><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mtext>q</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{i}\in{\{0,1\}^{(T+K+2)\times N}}\sim\mathcal{D}_{\text{q}}</annotation></semantics></math>. We construct the encoded prompt by (<a href="#S2.E2" title="In 2.2 Modeling ICL prediction with pre-trained LM ‣ 2 The Proposed Framework of Modeling Data Generation and Prediction ‣ A Framework for Quantifying How Pre-Training and Context Benefit In-Context Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>), which can be written as: <math id="A3.p2.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="U_{\text{stacked}}=(U_{1:n},\widetilde{U}_{\text{q}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mtext>stacked</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>U</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mtext>q</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{\text{stacked}}=(U_{1:n},\widetilde{U}_{\text{q}})</annotation></semantics></math>,
where the last <math id="A3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> columns in <math id="A3.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{U}_{\text{q}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>U</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mtext>q</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{U}_{\text{q}}</annotation></semantics></math> represent masks. We predict the masks as <math id="A3.p2.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\widehat{y}_{\text{q}}=f_{\bf w}\left(\mathbf{Z}\right)_{1:D,nN+L_{1}+1:N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mtext>q</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝐰</mi></msub><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{y}_{\text{q}}=f_{\bf w}\left(\mathbf{Z}\right)_{1:D,nN+L_{1}+1:N}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmclaim2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_claim">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmclaim2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Claim 2</span></span><span id="Thmclaim2.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmclaim2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmclaim2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmclaim2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">(Formal Version) Generate each encoded pre-train data <math id="Thmclaim2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{\text{train}}\sim\mathcal{D}_{\text{train}},\widetilde{U}_{\text{train}}\sim\widetilde{\mathcal{D}}_{\text{train}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">train</mtext></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">train</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>U</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">train</mtext></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">train</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{\text{train}}\sim\mathcal{D}_{\text{train}},\widetilde{U}_{\text{train}}\sim\widetilde{\mathcal{D}}_{\text{train}}</annotation></semantics></math>. There exists <math id="Thmclaim2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{1}&lt;a_{2}&lt;\cdots&lt;a_{n+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">&lt;</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.1389em">⋯</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em">&lt;</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{1}&lt;a_{2}&lt;\cdots&lt;a_{n+1}</annotation></semantics></math>, such that if we train a one-layer Transformer (<a href="#S2.E5" title="In 2.3 Comparing proposed context construction with existing works ‣ 2 The Proposed Framework of Modeling Data Generation and Prediction ‣ A Framework for Quantifying How Pre-Training and Context Benefit In-Context Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>): (1) With attention <math id="Thmclaim2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> that satisfies Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption2" title="Assumption 2. ‣ 3.3 Pre-trained One-layer Transformer ‣ 3 A Statistical Model: Pre-trained Transformer Shifts the Output Distribution ‣ A Framework for Quantifying How Pre-Training and Context Benefit In-Context Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>; (2) By minimizing the <math id="Thmclaim2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>-regularized objective function (<a href="#S3.E9" title="In 3.2 Training Objective and Inference ‣ 3 A Statistical Model: Pre-trained Transformer Shifts the Output Distribution ‣ A Framework for Quantifying How Pre-Training and Context Benefit In-Context Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>) with variable <math id="Thmclaim2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{W}^{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>V</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{W}^{V}</annotation></semantics></math>. Suppose <math id="Thmclaim2.p1.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\boldsymbol{W}^{{V}*}\in\underset{\lambda\rightarrow 0}{\operatorname{lim}}\operatorname{argmax}L(\boldsymbol{W}^{V})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝐖</mi><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0.222em">∗</mo></mrow></msup><mo>∈</mo><munder accentunder="true"><mi>lim</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">λ</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em" stretchy="false">→</mo><mn mathsize="0.700em">0</mn></mrow></munder><mi>argmax</mi><mi>L</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>V</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{W}^{{V}*}\in\underset{\lambda\rightarrow 0}{\operatorname{lim}}\operatorname{argmax}L(\boldsymbol{W}^{V})</annotation></semantics></math>, and we use <math id="Thmclaim2.p1.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="f_{W^{\boldsymbol{V}*}}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>W</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>𝐕</mi><mo lspace="0.222em">∗</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{W^{\boldsymbol{V}*}}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> as prediction model. Given a masked query sequence <math id="Thmclaim2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{X}_{\text{q}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">q</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{X}_{\text{q}}</annotation></semantics></math> encoded as <math id="Thmclaim2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{U}_{\text{q}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>U</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">q</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{U}_{\text{q}}</annotation></semantics></math>, predict the last <math id="Thmclaim2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> tokens (<math id="Thmclaim2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{1}+1\leqslant j\leqslant N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>⩽</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{1}+1\leqslant j\leqslant N</annotation></semantics></math>) as <math id="Thmclaim2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{y}_{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>q</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{y}_{q}</annotation></semantics></math>. We have following :
<br class="ltx_break"></span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx33" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex39"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(1)\begin{cases}&amp;f_{\bf w}(\widetilde{U}_{\text{q}})_{l,j}=1/T,\;l=1,2,\cdots,T,\\
&amp;\underset{T+1\leqslant l\leqslant T+K+1}{\arg\max}f_{\bf w}(\widetilde{U}_{\text{q}})_{l,j}=T+k^{*}_{\text{q}}+1\end{cases}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi>f</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>𝐰</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>U</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">q</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>T</mi><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>max</mi></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">T</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">+</mo><mn mathsize="0.700em">1</mn></mrow><mo mathsize="0.700em">⩽</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">l</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">⩽</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">T</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">+</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">K</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">+</mo><mn mathsize="0.700em">1</mn></mrow></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝐰</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>U</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">q</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>k</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">q</mtext><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(1)\begin{cases}&amp;f_{\bf w}(\widetilde{U}_{\text{q}})_{l,j}=1/T,\;l=1,2,\cdots,T,\\
&amp;\underset{T+1\leqslant l\leqslant T+K+1}{\arg\max}f_{\bf w}(\widetilde{U}_{\text{q}})_{l,j}=T+k^{*}_{\text{q}}+1\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="A3.EGx34" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex40"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(2)\begin{cases}&amp;\underset{0\leqslant l\leqslant T}{\arg\max}\ f_{\bf w}({U}_{\text{stacked}})_{l,j}=t^{*}\\
&amp;\underset{T+1\leqslant l\leqslant T+K+1}{\arg\max}f_{\bf w}({U}_{\text{stacked}})_{l,j}=T+k^{*}_{\text{q}}+1\end{cases}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>max</mi></mrow><mrow><mn mathsize="0.700em">0</mn><mo mathsize="0.700em">⩽</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">l</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">⩽</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">T</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝐰</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">stacked</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>max</mi></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">T</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">+</mo><mn mathsize="0.700em">1</mn></mrow><mo mathsize="0.700em">⩽</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">l</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">⩽</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">T</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">+</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">K</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">+</mo><mn mathsize="0.700em">1</mn></mrow></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝐰</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">stacked</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>k</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">q</mtext><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(2)\begin{cases}&amp;\underset{0\leqslant l\leqslant T}{\arg\max}\ f_{\bf w}({U}_{\text{stacked}})_{l,j}=t^{*}\\
&amp;\underset{T+1\leqslant l\leqslant T+K+1}{\arg\max}f_{\bf w}({U}_{\text{stacked}})_{l,j}=T+k^{*}_{\text{q}}+1\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">First, let us derive the closed form of <math id="A3.p3.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{\boldsymbol{W}}^{V*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝑾</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0.222em">∗</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\boldsymbol{W}}^{V*}</annotation></semantics></math>. The proof idea follows from <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib19" title="" class="ltx_ref">Li et al., 2023b</a>]</cite>. For a document <math id="A3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{w}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒘</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{w}</annotation></semantics></math>, when the document length <math id="A3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> is large, for <math id="A3.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=0,1,\cdots,T+K+1,j\geqslant 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>⩾</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=0,1,\cdots,T+K+1,j\geqslant 2</annotation></semantics></math>. Define <math id="A3.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{1}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>𝟏</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{1}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> as the indicator function. We have the following equation:</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx35" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex41"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle[\widetilde{{X}}A(\widetilde{U})]_{lj}=\frac{1}{N}\sum_{p=1}^{N}\widetilde{U}_{lp}=\frac{1}{N}\sum_{p=1}^{N}\mathbf{1}_{\widetilde{U}_{lp}=1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>U</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>U</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>U</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle[\widetilde{{X}}A(\widetilde{U})]_{lj}=\frac{1}{N}\sum_{p=1}^{N}\widetilde{U}_{lp}=\frac{1}{N}\sum_{p=1}^{N}\mathbf{1}_{\widetilde{U}_{lp}=1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex42"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\begin{cases}p_{m}&amp;\text{ if }l=0\\
P_{\boldsymbol{w}}(l)\left(1-p_{m}\right)&amp;\text{ if }l\in[T]\\
p_{m}&amp;\text{ if }l=T+1\\
Q&amp;\text{ if }l=T+k^{*}+1\\
\frac{1-Q}{K-1}&amp;\text{ if }T+2\leqslant l\leqslant T+K+1,l\neq T+k^{*}+1\end{cases}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext> if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>𝒘</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext> if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext> if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mi>Q</mi></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext> if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext> if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mi>l</mi><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>≠</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\begin{cases}p_{m}&amp;\text{ if }l=0\\
P_{\boldsymbol{w}}(l)\left(1-p_{m}\right)&amp;\text{ if }l\in[T]\\
p_{m}&amp;\text{ if }l=T+1\\
Q&amp;\text{ if }l=T+k^{*}+1\\
\frac{1-Q}{K-1}&amp;\text{ if }T+2\leqslant l\leqslant T+K+1,l\neq T+k^{*}+1\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">The prediction of the <math id="A3.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math>-th column can be written as following:</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx36" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex43"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\quad(\boldsymbol{W}\widetilde{{U}}A(\widetilde{{U}}))_{lj}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑾</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>U</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>U</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad(\boldsymbol{W}\widetilde{{U}}A(\widetilde{{U}}))_{lj}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex44"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\begin{cases}\boldsymbol{W}_{l0}p_{m}+\sum\limits_{r=1}^{T}\boldsymbol{W}_{lr}P_{\boldsymbol{w}}(r)(1-p_{m})&amp;\text{ if }l\in[T]\\
\boldsymbol{W}_{l0}p_{m}+\sum\limits_{l=1}^{T}\boldsymbol{W}_{lr}P_{\boldsymbol{w}}(r\mid X_{1})(1-p_{m})&amp;\text{ if }T+1\leqslant l\leqslant T+K+1\end{cases}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝑾</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>𝑾</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>𝒘</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext> if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝑾</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>𝑾</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>𝒘</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext> if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mi>l</mi><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\begin{cases}\boldsymbol{W}_{l0}p_{m}+\sum\limits_{r=1}^{T}\boldsymbol{W}_{lr}P_{\boldsymbol{w}}(r)(1-p_{m})&amp;\text{ if }l\in[T]\\
\boldsymbol{W}_{l0}p_{m}+\sum\limits_{l=1}^{T}\boldsymbol{W}_{lr}P_{\boldsymbol{w}}(r\mid X_{1})(1-p_{m})&amp;\text{ if }T+1\leqslant l\leqslant T+K+1\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text">Recall the loss function is</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx37" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E12.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle L(\boldsymbol{W})=\mathbb{E}_{U\sim\mathcal{D}_{\text{train}}}\frac{1}{N}\sum_{j=1}^{N}\left\|(\boldsymbol{W}\widetilde{U}A(\widetilde{U}))_{:j}-X_{:j}\right\|_{2}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝑾</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mtext>train</mtext></msub></mrow></msub><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝑾</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>U</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>U</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle L(\boldsymbol{W})=\mathbb{E}_{U\sim\mathcal{D}_{\text{train}}}\frac{1}{N}\sum_{j=1}^{N}\left\|(\boldsymbol{W}\widetilde{U}A(\widetilde{U}))_{:j}-X_{:j}\right\|_{2}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(12)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p3.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p3.4.1" class="ltx_text">It is easy to show that <math id="A3.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\forall U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\forall U</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L(\boldsymbol{W})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝑾</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L(\boldsymbol{W})</annotation></semantics></math> is minimized at</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx38" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex45"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex45.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle(\boldsymbol{W}\widetilde{U}A(\widetilde{U}))_{:j}=\frac{1}{N}\sum_{p=1}^{N}U_{:p}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝑾</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>U</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>U</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>U</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(\boldsymbol{W}\widetilde{U}A(\widetilde{U}))_{:j}=\frac{1}{N}\sum_{p=1}^{N}U_{:p},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p3.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p3.5.1" class="ltx_text">which is equivalent to</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx39" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex46"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex46.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{cases}&amp;(\boldsymbol{W}\widetilde{U}A(\widetilde{U}))_{0j}=0\\
&amp;(\boldsymbol{W}\widetilde{U}A(\widetilde{U}))_{lj}=P_{\boldsymbol{w}}(i),\quad i\in[T]\\
&amp;(\boldsymbol{W}\widetilde{U}A(\widetilde{U}))_{T+1,j}=0.\\
&amp;(\boldsymbol{W}\widetilde{U}A(\widetilde{U}))_{lj}=P_{\boldsymbol{w}}(l\mid U_{1}),\quad T+2\leqslant l\leqslant T+K+1\end{cases}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑾</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>U</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>U</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑾</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>U</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>U</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>𝒘</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑾</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>U</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>U</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑾</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>U</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>U</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>𝒘</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mi>l</mi><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{cases}&amp;(\boldsymbol{W}\widetilde{U}A(\widetilde{U}))_{0j}=0\\
&amp;(\boldsymbol{W}\widetilde{U}A(\widetilde{U}))_{lj}=P_{\boldsymbol{w}}(i),\quad i\in[T]\\
&amp;(\boldsymbol{W}\widetilde{U}A(\widetilde{U}))_{T+1,j}=0.\\
&amp;(\boldsymbol{W}\widetilde{U}A(\widetilde{U}))_{lj}=P_{\boldsymbol{w}}(l\mid U_{1}),\quad T+2\leqslant l\leqslant T+K+1\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p3.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p3.6.1" class="ltx_text">(1) Consider the first <math id="A3.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T+1</annotation></semantics></math> rows.</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx40" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{cases}\boldsymbol{W}_{00}p_{m}+\sum\limits_{r=1}^{T}\boldsymbol{W}_{0l}P_{\boldsymbol{w}}(r)(1-p_{m})=0\\
\boldsymbol{W}_{l0}p_{m}+\sum\limits_{r=1}^{T}\boldsymbol{W}_{lr}P_{\boldsymbol{w}}(r)(1-p_{m})=P_{\boldsymbol{w}}(l)\text{ if }l\in[T].\end{cases}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝑾</mi><mn>00</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>𝑾</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>𝒘</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝑾</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>𝑾</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>𝒘</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>𝒘</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{cases}\boldsymbol{W}_{00}p_{m}+\sum\limits_{r=1}^{T}\boldsymbol{W}_{0l}P_{\boldsymbol{w}}(r)(1-p_{m})=0\\
\boldsymbol{W}_{l0}p_{m}+\sum\limits_{r=1}^{T}\boldsymbol{W}_{lr}P_{\boldsymbol{w}}(r)(1-p_{m})=P_{\boldsymbol{w}}(l)\text{ if }l\in[T].\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(13)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p3.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p3.7.1" class="ltx_text">We claim that <math id="A3.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\forall l" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\forall l</annotation></semantics></math>, there exists <math id="A3.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{l}</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A3.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\forall r\neq l" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\forall r\neq l</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.p3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{W}_{lj}=u_{l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝑾</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{W}_{lj}=u_{l}</annotation></semantics></math>.
We prove the claim by contradiction. Suppose the above claim does not hold. We consider a special case where topic <math id="A3.p3.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="`1^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>`</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">`1^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> is selected topic in Step 1 in data generation Section <a href="#S3.SS1" title="3.1 Data Generation and Encoding ‣ 3 A Statistical Model: Pre-trained Transformer Shifts the Output Distribution ‣ A Framework for Quantifying How Pre-Training and Context Benefit In-Context Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a>. Then the following equations hold:</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx41" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex47"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex47.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{cases}&amp;P_{\boldsymbol{w}}(1)=\frac{1}{2}=\boldsymbol{W}_{10}p_{m}+\boldsymbol{W}_{12}\cdot\frac{1}{2}\cdot(1-p_{m}),\quad\text{if $`1^{\prime}$ and $`2^{\prime}$ are selected},\\
&amp;P_{\boldsymbol{w}}(1)=\frac{1}{2}=\boldsymbol{W}_{10}p_{m}+\boldsymbol{W}_{13}\cdot\frac{1}{2}\cdot(1-p_{m}),\quad\text{if $`1^{\prime}$ and $`3^{\prime}$ are selected}.\end{cases}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>𝒘</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝑾</mi><mn>10</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑾</mi><mn>12</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mrow><mi>`</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mtext> and </mtext><mrow><mi>`</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mtext> are selected</mtext></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>𝒘</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝑾</mi><mn>10</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑾</mi><mn>13</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mrow><mi>`</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mtext> and </mtext><mrow><mi>`</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mn>3</mn><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mtext> are selected</mtext></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{cases}&amp;P_{\boldsymbol{w}}(1)=\frac{1}{2}=\boldsymbol{W}_{10}p_{m}+\boldsymbol{W}_{12}\cdot\frac{1}{2}\cdot(1-p_{m}),\quad\text{if $`1^{\prime}$ and $`2^{\prime}$ are selected},\\
&amp;P_{\boldsymbol{w}}(1)=\frac{1}{2}=\boldsymbol{W}_{10}p_{m}+\boldsymbol{W}_{13}\cdot\frac{1}{2}\cdot(1-p_{m}),\quad\text{if $`1^{\prime}$ and $`3^{\prime}$ are selected}.\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p3.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p3.8.1" class="ltx_text">Suppose the above two equations need to hold, then there is <math id="A3.p3.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{W}_{12}=\boldsymbol{W}_{13}=u_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝑾</mi><mn>12</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝑾</mi><mn>13</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{W}_{12}=\boldsymbol{W}_{13}=u_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>. Similarly, <math id="A3.p3.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\forall l" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\forall l</annotation></semantics></math>, there exists <math id="A3.p3.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{l}=\boldsymbol{W}_{lr},\;r\neq l" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝑾</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{l}=\boldsymbol{W}_{lr},\;r\neq l</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, (<a href="#A3.E13" title="In Proof. ‣ Appendix C Proof of Claim ‣ A Framework for Quantifying How Pre-Training and Context Benefit In-Context Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a>) can be written as:</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx42" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex48"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex48.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{cases}&amp;\boldsymbol{W}_{00}=-\frac{u_{0}(1-p_{m})}{p_{m}}\\
&amp;\boldsymbol{W}_{l0}p_{m}+u_{l}(1-p_{m})+P_{\boldsymbol{w}}(l)\left(\boldsymbol{W}_{ll}(1-p_{m})-u_{l}(1-p_{m})-1\right)=0\end{cases}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><msub><mi>𝑾</mi><mn>00</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝑾</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>𝒘</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝑾</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{cases}&amp;\boldsymbol{W}_{00}=-\frac{u_{0}(1-p_{m})}{p_{m}}\\
&amp;\boldsymbol{W}_{l0}p_{m}+u_{l}(1-p_{m})+P_{\boldsymbol{w}}(l)\left(\boldsymbol{W}_{ll}(1-p_{m})-u_{l}(1-p_{m})-1\right)=0\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p3.9" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p3.9.1" class="ltx_text">Then we have</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx43" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex49"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex49.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{cases}&amp;\boldsymbol{W}_{00}=-\frac{u_{0}(1-p_{m})}{p_{m}}\\
&amp;\boldsymbol{W}_{ll}=u_{l}+\frac{1}{1-p_{m}}\\
&amp;\boldsymbol{W}_{l0}=-\frac{u_{l}(1-p_{m})}{p_{m}}\end{cases}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><msub><mi>𝑾</mi><mn>00</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><msub><mi>𝑾</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><msub><mi>𝑾</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{cases}&amp;\boldsymbol{W}_{00}=-\frac{u_{0}(1-p_{m})}{p_{m}}\\
&amp;\boldsymbol{W}_{ll}=u_{l}+\frac{1}{1-p_{m}}\\
&amp;\boldsymbol{W}_{l0}=-\frac{u_{l}(1-p_{m})}{p_{m}}\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p3.10" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p3.10.1" class="ltx_text">(2) Consider the last <math id="A3.p3.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K+1</annotation></semantics></math> rows.</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx44" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{cases}&amp;\boldsymbol{W}_{T+1,0}p_{m}+\sum\limits_{r=T+1}^{T+K+1}\boldsymbol{W}_{T+1,l}P_{\boldsymbol{w}}(r\mid U_{1})\left(1-p_{m}\right)=0\\
&amp;\boldsymbol{W}_{l0}p_{m}+\sum\limits_{r=T+2}^{T+K+1}\boldsymbol{W}_{lr}P_{\boldsymbol{w}}(l\mid U_{1})(1-p_{m})=P_{\boldsymbol{w}}(l\mid U_{1})\end{cases}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝑾</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>𝑾</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>𝒘</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝑾</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>𝑾</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>𝒘</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>𝒘</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{cases}&amp;\boldsymbol{W}_{T+1,0}p_{m}+\sum\limits_{r=T+1}^{T+K+1}\boldsymbol{W}_{T+1,l}P_{\boldsymbol{w}}(r\mid U_{1})\left(1-p_{m}\right)=0\\
&amp;\boldsymbol{W}_{l0}p_{m}+\sum\limits_{r=T+2}^{T+K+1}\boldsymbol{W}_{lr}P_{\boldsymbol{w}}(l\mid U_{1})(1-p_{m})=P_{\boldsymbol{w}}(l\mid U_{1})\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(14)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p3.11" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p3.11.1" class="ltx_text">Now we claim, <math id="A3.p3.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\forall r\neq l" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\forall r\neq l</annotation></semantics></math>, there exists <math id="A3.p3.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{l}</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A3.p3.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{W}_{lr}=q_{l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝑾</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{W}_{lr}=q_{l}</annotation></semantics></math>. We prove the claim by contradiction. Suppose <math id="A3.p3.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l\neq k^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>≠</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l\neq k^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="A3.p3.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\forall Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\forall Q</annotation></semantics></math>, we have the following equation:</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx45" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex50"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex50.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{cases}&amp;\frac{1-Q}{K-1}=\boldsymbol{W}_{l0}p_{m}+\boldsymbol{W}_{ll_{1}}Q(1-p_{m})+\sum\limits_{r\neq l_{1}}\boldsymbol{W}_{rl_{1}}\cdot\frac{1-Q}{K-1}(1-p_{m}),\quad\text{$\text{key class}=l_{1}$}\\
&amp;\frac{1-Q}{K-1}=\boldsymbol{W}_{l0}p_{m}+\boldsymbol{W}_{ll_{2}}Q(1-p_{m})+\sum\limits_{r\neq l_{2}}\boldsymbol{W}_{rl_{2}}\cdot\frac{1-Q}{K-1}(1-p_{m}),\quad\text{$\text{key class}=l_{2}$}.\end{cases}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝑾</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑾</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>l</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>≠</mo><msub><mi>l</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></munder><msub><mi>𝑾</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>l</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mtext>key class</mtext><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>l</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝑾</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑾</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>l</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>≠</mo><msub><mi>l</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></munder><msub><mi>𝑾</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>l</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mtext>key class</mtext><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>l</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{cases}&amp;\frac{1-Q}{K-1}=\boldsymbol{W}_{l0}p_{m}+\boldsymbol{W}_{ll_{1}}Q(1-p_{m})+\sum\limits_{r\neq l_{1}}\boldsymbol{W}_{rl_{1}}\cdot\frac{1-Q}{K-1}(1-p_{m}),\quad\text{$\text{key class}=l_{1}$}\\
&amp;\frac{1-Q}{K-1}=\boldsymbol{W}_{l0}p_{m}+\boldsymbol{W}_{ll_{2}}Q(1-p_{m})+\sum\limits_{r\neq l_{2}}\boldsymbol{W}_{rl_{2}}\cdot\frac{1-Q}{K-1}(1-p_{m}),\quad\text{$\text{key class}=l_{2}$}.\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p3.12" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p3.12.1" class="ltx_text">Thus, we must have <math id="A3.p3.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{W}_{ll_{1}}=\boldsymbol{W}_{ll_{2}}=q_{l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝑾</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>l</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝑾</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>l</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{W}_{ll_{1}}=\boldsymbol{W}_{ll_{2}}=q_{l}</annotation></semantics></math>. We can rewrite (<a href="#A3.E14" title="In Proof. ‣ Appendix C Proof of Claim ‣ A Framework for Quantifying How Pre-Training and Context Benefit In-Context Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">14</span></a>) as following:</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx46" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex51"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex51.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{cases}&amp;\boldsymbol{W}_{T+1,0}p_{m}+q_{T+1}(1-p_{m})=0\\
&amp;\boldsymbol{W}_{l0}p_{m}+\boldsymbol{W}_{ll}P_{\boldsymbol{w}}(l\mid X_{1})(1-p_{m})+q_{l}\left(1-P_{\boldsymbol{w}}(l\mid U_{1})\right)(1-p_{m})=P_{\boldsymbol{w}}\left(l\mid U_{1}\right)\end{cases}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝑾</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝑾</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑾</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>𝒘</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>𝒘</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>𝒘</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{cases}&amp;\boldsymbol{W}_{T+1,0}p_{m}+q_{T+1}(1-p_{m})=0\\
&amp;\boldsymbol{W}_{l0}p_{m}+\boldsymbol{W}_{ll}P_{\boldsymbol{w}}(l\mid X_{1})(1-p_{m})+q_{l}\left(1-P_{\boldsymbol{w}}(l\mid U_{1})\right)(1-p_{m})=P_{\boldsymbol{w}}\left(l\mid U_{1}\right)\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p3.13" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p3.13.1" class="ltx_text">Then we have</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx47" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex52"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex52.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{cases}&amp;\boldsymbol{W}_{T+1,0}=-\frac{q_{T+2}\left(1-p_{m}\right)}{p_{m}}\\
&amp;\boldsymbol{W}_{ll}=q_{i}+\frac{1}{1-p_{m}}\\
&amp;\boldsymbol{W}_{l0}=-\frac{q_{l}\left(1-p_{m}\right)}{p_{m}}\end{cases}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><msub><mi>𝑾</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><msub><mi>𝑾</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><msub><mi>𝑾</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{cases}&amp;\boldsymbol{W}_{T+1,0}=-\frac{q_{T+2}\left(1-p_{m}\right)}{p_{m}}\\
&amp;\boldsymbol{W}_{ll}=q_{i}+\frac{1}{1-p_{m}}\\
&amp;\boldsymbol{W}_{l0}=-\frac{q_{l}\left(1-p_{m}\right)}{p_{m}}\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p3.14" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p3.14.1" class="ltx_text">By Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma1" title="Lemma 1. ‣ Appendix C Proof of Claim ‣ A Framework for Quantifying How Pre-Training and Context Benefit In-Context Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, it suffices to find <math id="A3.p3.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{l},q_{l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{l},q_{l}</annotation></semantics></math> that minimizes <math id="A3.p3.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\boldsymbol{W}^{V}\|_{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msup><mi>𝑾</mi><mi>V</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\boldsymbol{W}^{V}\|_{F}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Now consider the first <math id="A3.p3.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T+1</annotation></semantics></math> rows of <math id="A3.p3.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{W}^{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝑾</mi><mi>V</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{W}^{V}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx48" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex53"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex53.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\|\boldsymbol{W}^{V}_{0:T,:}\|_{F}^{2}=\frac{u_{0}^{2}\left(1-p_{m}\right)^{2}}{p_{m}^{2}}+Tu_{0}^{2}+\sum\limits_{l=1}^{T}\frac{u_{l}^{2}\left(1-p_{m}\right)^{2}}{p_{m}^{2}}+(T-1)u_{l}^{2}+\left(\frac{1}{1-p_{m}}+u_{l}\right)^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑾</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>:</mo></mrow><mi>V</mi></msubsup><msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0.0835em">=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mi>T</mi><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mi>l</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mi>l</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|\boldsymbol{W}^{V}_{0:T,:}\|_{F}^{2}=\frac{u_{0}^{2}\left(1-p_{m}\right)^{2}}{p_{m}^{2}}+Tu_{0}^{2}+\sum\limits_{l=1}^{T}\frac{u_{l}^{2}\left(1-p_{m}\right)^{2}}{p_{m}^{2}}+(T-1)u_{l}^{2}+\left(\frac{1}{1-p_{m}}+u_{l}\right)^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p3.15" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p3.15.1" class="ltx_text">It is easy to derive that <math id="A3.p3.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{0}^{*}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{0}^{*}=0</annotation></semantics></math>. For <math id="A3.p3.m30" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l=1,2,\cdots,T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l=1,2,\cdots,T</annotation></semantics></math>, we take the derivative</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx49" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex54"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex54.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\quad\frac{\partial\|\boldsymbol{W}_{l,:}\|^{2}_{F}}{\partial u_{l}}=2\left(\frac{u_{l}(1-p_{m})^{2}}{p_{m}^{2}}+(T-1)u_{l}+u_{l}+\frac{1}{1-p_{m}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>𝑾</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>:</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em">∥</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad\frac{\partial\|\boldsymbol{W}_{l,:}\|^{2}_{F}}{\partial u_{l}}=2\left(\frac{u_{l}(1-p_{m})^{2}}{p_{m}^{2}}+(T-1)u_{l}+u_{l}+\frac{1}{1-p_{m}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex55"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex55.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=2\left(\left(T+\frac{(1-p_{m})^{2}}{p_{m}^{2}}\right)u_{l}+\frac{1}{1-p_{m}}\right)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=2\left(\left(T+\frac{(1-p_{m})^{2}}{p_{m}^{2}}\right)u_{l}+\frac{1}{1-p_{m}}\right)=0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p3.16" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p3.16.1" class="ltx_text">So we derive</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx50" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{cases}&amp;u_{l}=-\frac{1}{(1-p_{m})\cdot\left(T+\frac{(1-p_{m})^{2}}{p_{m}^{2}}\right)}=u^{*}\\
&amp;\boldsymbol{W}_{ll}=u_{i}+\frac{1}{1-p_{m}}=u^{*}+\frac{1}{1-p_{m}}\\
&amp;\boldsymbol{W}_{l0}=\frac{-u_{l}(1-p_{m})}{p_{m}}=\frac{-u^{*}(1-p_{m})}{p_{m}}\end{cases}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><msub><mi>𝑾</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><msub><mi>𝑾</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{cases}&amp;u_{l}=-\frac{1}{(1-p_{m})\cdot\left(T+\frac{(1-p_{m})^{2}}{p_{m}^{2}}\right)}=u^{*}\\
&amp;\boldsymbol{W}_{ll}=u_{i}+\frac{1}{1-p_{m}}=u^{*}+\frac{1}{1-p_{m}}\\
&amp;\boldsymbol{W}_{l0}=\frac{-u_{l}(1-p_{m})}{p_{m}}=\frac{-u^{*}(1-p_{m})}{p_{m}}\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p3.17" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p3.17.1" class="ltx_text">Similarly, for the last <math id="A3.p3.m31" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K+1</annotation></semantics></math> rows, we have</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx51" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E16"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{cases}&amp;q_{l}=\frac{1}{\left(1-p_{m}\right)\cdot\left(K+\frac{\left(1-p_{m}\right)^{2}}{p_{m}^{2}}\right)}=q^{*}\\
&amp;\boldsymbol{W}_{ll}=q_{l}+\frac{1}{1-p_{m}}=q^{*}+\frac{1}{1-p_{m}}\\
&amp;\boldsymbol{W}_{l0}=\frac{-q_{l}\left(1-p_{m}\right)}{p_{m}}=\frac{-q^{*}\left(1-p_{m}\right)}{p_{m}}\end{cases}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><msub><mi>𝑾</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><msub><mi>𝑾</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{cases}&amp;q_{l}=\frac{1}{\left(1-p_{m}\right)\cdot\left(K+\frac{\left(1-p_{m}\right)^{2}}{p_{m}^{2}}\right)}=q^{*}\\
&amp;\boldsymbol{W}_{ll}=q_{l}+\frac{1}{1-p_{m}}=q^{*}+\frac{1}{1-p_{m}}\\
&amp;\boldsymbol{W}_{l0}=\frac{-q_{l}\left(1-p_{m}\right)}{p_{m}}=\frac{-q^{*}\left(1-p_{m}\right)}{p_{m}}\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(16)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p3.18" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p3.18.1" class="ltx_text">Up to now we have characterized the optimal solution <math id="A3.p3.m32" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\boldsymbol{W}^{V*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝑾</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0.222em">∗</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{W}^{V*}</annotation></semantics></math>. In the following part, we will compare the prediction with or without the prompt.
Given input <math id="A3.p3.m33" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{X}_{\text{q}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mtext>q</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{X}_{\text{q}}</annotation></semantics></math>, recall that our goal is to predict the last <math id="A3.p3.m34" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> masked columns in <math id="A3.p3.m35" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{U}_{\text{q}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>U</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mtext>q</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{U}_{\text{q}}</annotation></semantics></math>. For <math id="A3.p3.m36" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\forall L_{1}+1\leqslant j\leqslant N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>⩽</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\forall L_{1}+1\leqslant j\leqslant N</annotation></semantics></math> we have the following equation:</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx52" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex56"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex56.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle f_{\bf w}\left(\widetilde{U}_{\text{q}}\right)_{:,j}=\boldsymbol{W}^{V*}\cdot\widetilde{U}_{\text{q}}\cdot\left(A(\widetilde{U}_{\text{q}})\right)_{:,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝐰</mi></msub><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>U</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mtext>q</mtext></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>𝑾</mi><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0.222em">∗</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>U</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mtext>q</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>U</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mtext>q</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle f_{\bf w}\left(\widetilde{U}_{\text{q}}\right)_{:,j}=\boldsymbol{W}^{V*}\cdot\widetilde{U}_{\text{q}}\cdot\left(A(\widetilde{U}_{\text{q}})\right)_{:,j}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex57"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex57.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\boldsymbol{W}^{V*}\cdot\widetilde{U}_{\text{q}}\cdot\left(\frac{1}{N},\cdots,\frac{1}{N}\right)^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>𝑾</mi><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0.222em">∗</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>U</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mtext>q</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\boldsymbol{W}^{V*}\cdot\widetilde{U}_{\text{q}}\cdot\left(\frac{1}{N},\cdots,\frac{1}{N}\right)^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E17"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E17.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\boldsymbol{W}^{V*}\cdot\left(\frac{1}{N}\sum\limits_{p=1}^{N}\boldsymbol{1}_{\left({\widetilde{U}}_{\text{q}}\right)_{0p}=1},\cdots,\frac{1}{N}\sum\limits_{p=1}^{N}\boldsymbol{1}_{\left({\widetilde{U}}_{\text{q}}\right)_{T+K+1,p}=1}\right)^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>𝑾</mi><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0.222em">∗</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>U</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mtext>q</mtext></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>U</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mtext>q</mtext></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\boldsymbol{W}^{V*}\cdot\left(\frac{1}{N}\sum\limits_{p=1}^{N}\boldsymbol{1}_{\left({\widetilde{U}}_{\text{q}}\right)_{0p}=1},\cdots,\frac{1}{N}\sum\limits_{p=1}^{N}\boldsymbol{1}_{\left({\widetilde{U}}_{\text{q}}\right)_{T+K+1,p}=1}\right)^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(17)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p3.19" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p3.19.1" class="ltx_text">First, let us consider the first <math id="A3.p3.m37" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T+1</annotation></semantics></math> rows in the above prediction (<a href="#A3.E17" title="In Proof. ‣ Appendix C Proof of Claim ‣ A Framework for Quantifying How Pre-Training and Context Benefit In-Context Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">17</span></a>), which is the the topic predictor. Since we consider the case where the sequence length <math id="A3.p3.m38" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> goes infinity, we have</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx53" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex58"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex58.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle f_{\bf w}\left(\widetilde{U}_{\text{q}}\right)_{0:T,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝐰</mi></msub><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>U</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mtext>q</mtext></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle f_{\bf w}\left(\widetilde{U}_{\text{q}}\right)_{0:T,j}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex58.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\boldsymbol{W}^{V*}\cdot\left(\frac{1}{N}\sum\limits_{p=1}^{N}\boldsymbol{1}_{\left({\widetilde{U}}_{\text{q}}\right)_{0p}=1},\cdots,\frac{1}{N}\sum\limits_{p=1}^{N}\boldsymbol{1}_{\left({\widetilde{U}}_{\text{q}}\right)_{T+K+1,p}=1}\right)_{0:T}^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>𝑾</mi><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0.222em">∗</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>U</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mtext>q</mtext></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>U</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mtext>q</mtext></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\boldsymbol{W}^{V*}\cdot\left(\frac{1}{N}\sum\limits_{p=1}^{N}\boldsymbol{1}_{\left({\widetilde{U}}_{\text{q}}\right)_{0p}=1},\cdots,\frac{1}{N}\sum\limits_{p=1}^{N}\boldsymbol{1}_{\left({\widetilde{U}}_{\text{q}}\right)_{T+K+1,p}=1}\right)_{0:T}^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex59"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex59.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\boldsymbol{W}^{V*}\cdot\left(p_{m},\frac{1-p_{m}}{T},\cdots,\frac{1-p_{m}}{T}\right)^{\top}\in\mathbb{R}^{T+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>𝑾</mi><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0.222em">∗</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\boldsymbol{W}^{V*}\cdot\left(p_{m},\frac{1-p_{m}}{T},\cdots,\frac{1-p_{m}}{T}\right)^{\top}\in\mathbb{R}^{T+1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p3.20" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p3.20.1" class="ltx_text">Recall the optimal <math id="A3.p3.m39" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\boldsymbol{W}^{V*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝑾</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0.222em">∗</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{W}^{V*}</annotation></semantics></math>. For <math id="A3.p3.m40" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l\in[T]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l\in[T]</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx54" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex60"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex60.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\boldsymbol{W}^{V*}\cdot\left(p_{m},\frac{1-p_{m}}{T},\cdots,\frac{1-p_{m}}{T}\right)_{l}^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝑾</mi><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0.222em">∗</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\boldsymbol{W}^{V*}\cdot\left(p_{m},\frac{1-p_{m}}{T},\cdots,\frac{1-p_{m}}{T}\right)_{l}^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex61"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex61.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{-u^{*}(1-p_{m})}{p_{m}}\cdot p_{m}+\left(u^{*}+\frac{1}{1-p_{m}}\right)\cdot\frac{1-p_{m}}{T}+(T-1)u^{*}\cdot\frac{1-p_{m}}{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{-u^{*}(1-p_{m})}{p_{m}}\cdot p_{m}+\left(u^{*}+\frac{1}{1-p_{m}}\right)\cdot\frac{1-p_{m}}{T}+(T-1)u^{*}\cdot\frac{1-p_{m}}{T}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex62"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex62.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{T}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p3.21" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p3.21.1" class="ltx_text">The result implies that the predicted topics have the same probability.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Second, we consider the class predictor in (<a href="#A3.E17" title="In Proof. ‣ Appendix C Proof of Claim ‣ A Framework for Quantifying How Pre-Training and Context Benefit In-Context Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">17</span></a>), which is the last <math id="A3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K+1</annotation></semantics></math> rows in (<a href="#A3.E17" title="In Proof. ‣ Appendix C Proof of Claim ‣ A Framework for Quantifying How Pre-Training and Context Benefit In-Context Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">17</span></a>). For simplicity, we consider the case where the key word class <math id="A3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k^{*}_{\text{q}}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>k</mi><mtext>q</mtext><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k^{*}_{\text{q}}=1</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx55" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex63"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex63.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle f_{\bf w}\left(\widetilde{U}_{\text{q}}\right)_{T+1:T+K+1,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝐰</mi></msub><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>U</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mtext>q</mtext></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle f_{\bf w}\left(\widetilde{U}_{\text{q}}\right)_{T+1:T+K+1,j}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex63.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\boldsymbol{W}^{V*}\cdot\left(\frac{1}{N}\sum\limits_{p=1}^{N}\boldsymbol{1}_{\left({\widetilde{U}}_{\text{q}}\right)_{0p}=1},\cdots,\frac{1}{N}\sum\limits_{p=1}^{N}\boldsymbol{1}_{\left({\widetilde{U}}_{\text{q}}\right)_{T+K+1,p}=1}\right)_{T+1:T+K+1}^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>𝑾</mi><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0.222em">∗</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>U</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mtext>q</mtext></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>U</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mtext>q</mtext></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\boldsymbol{W}^{V*}\cdot\left(\frac{1}{N}\sum\limits_{p=1}^{N}\boldsymbol{1}_{\left({\widetilde{U}}_{\text{q}}\right)_{0p}=1},\cdots,\frac{1}{N}\sum\limits_{p=1}^{N}\boldsymbol{1}_{\left({\widetilde{U}}_{\text{q}}\right)_{T+K+1,p}=1}\right)_{T+1:T+K+1}^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex64"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex64.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\boldsymbol{W}^{V*}\cdot\left(p_{m},Q(1-p_{m}),\frac{1-Q}{K-1}(1-p_{m}),\cdots\frac{1-Q}{K-1}(1-p_{m})\right)^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>𝑾</mi><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0.222em">∗</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\boldsymbol{W}^{V*}\cdot\left(p_{m},Q(1-p_{m}),\frac{1-Q}{K-1}(1-p_{m}),\cdots\frac{1-Q}{K-1}(1-p_{m})\right)^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">For <math id="A3.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l=T+k^{*}_{\text{q}}+1=T+K+2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>k</mi><mtext>q</mtext><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l=T+k^{*}_{\text{q}}+1=T+K+2</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx56" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex65"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex65.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle f_{\bf w}\left(\widetilde{U}_{\text{q }}\right)_{l,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝐰</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>U</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mtext>q </mtext></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle f_{\bf w}\left(\widetilde{U}_{\text{q }}\right)_{l,j}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex65.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{-v^{*}\left(1-p_{m}\right)}{p_{m}}\cdot p_{m}+\left(v^{*}+\frac{1}{1-p_{m}}\right)\cdot Q(1-p_{m})+(K-1)\cdot v_{i}\cdot\frac{1-Q}{K-1}\left(1-p_{m}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{-v^{*}\left(1-p_{m}\right)}{p_{m}}\cdot p_{m}+\left(v^{*}+\frac{1}{1-p_{m}}\right)\cdot Q(1-p_{m})+(K-1)\cdot v_{i}\cdot\frac{1-Q}{K-1}\left(1-p_{m}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex66"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex66.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=-v^{*}\left(1-p_{m}\right)+v^{*}\cdot Q(1-p_{m})+Q+v^{*}(1-Q)(1-p_{m})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-v^{*}\left(1-p_{m}\right)+v^{*}\cdot Q(1-p_{m})+Q+v^{*}(1-Q)(1-p_{m})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex67"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex67.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=Q</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p4.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p4.3.1" class="ltx_text">Similarly, we can compute that for <math id="A3.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l\neq T+K+2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>≠</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l\neq T+K+2</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx57" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex68"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex68.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle f_{\bf w}\left(\widetilde{U}_{\text{q}}\right)_{l,j}=\frac{1-Q}{K-1}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝐰</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>U</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mtext>q</mtext></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle f_{\bf w}\left(\widetilde{U}_{\text{q}}\right)_{l,j}=\frac{1-Q}{K-1}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Next, we consider the case where we have the in-context samples <math id="A3.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{1},s_{2},\cdots,s_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{1},s_{2},\cdots,s_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx58" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex69"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex69.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle f_{\bf w}\left(U_{\text{stacked}}\right)_{:,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝐰</mi></msub><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mtext>stacked</mtext></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle f_{\bf w}\left(U_{\text{stacked}}\right)_{:,j}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex69.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\boldsymbol{W}^{V*}\cdot U_{\text{stacked}}\cdot\left(A(U_{\text{stacked}})\right)_{:,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>𝑾</mi><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0.222em">∗</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mtext>stacked</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mtext>stacked</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\boldsymbol{W}^{V*}\cdot U_{\text{stacked}}\cdot\left(A(U_{\text{stacked}})\right)_{:,j}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E18"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E18.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\boldsymbol{W}^{V*}\cdot\left(U_{1},\cdots,U_{n},\widetilde{U}_{\text{q}}\right)\cdot\left(a_{1}/N,\cdots,a_{1}/N,a_{2}/N,\cdots,a_{2}/N,\cdots,a_{n+1}/N,\cdots,a_{n+1}/N\right)^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>𝑾</mi><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0.222em">∗</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>U</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mtext>q</mtext></msub><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\boldsymbol{W}^{V*}\cdot\left(U_{1},\cdots,U_{n},\widetilde{U}_{\text{q}}\right)\cdot\left(a_{1}/N,\cdots,a_{1}/N,a_{2}/N,\cdots,a_{2}/N,\cdots,a_{n+1}/N,\cdots,a_{n+1}/N\right)^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(18)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">Similarly, we consider the first <math id="A3.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T+1</annotation></semantics></math> entries in (<a href="#A3.E18" title="In Proof. ‣ Appendix C Proof of Claim ‣ A Framework for Quantifying How Pre-Training and Context Benefit In-Context Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">18</span></a>), which is the topic predictor. Recall the query distribution defined in Section <a href="#S3.SS1" title="3.1 Data Generation and Encoding ‣ 3 A Statistical Model: Pre-trained Transformer Shifts the Output Distribution ‣ A Framework for Quantifying How Pre-Training and Context Benefit In-Context Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a>,</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx59" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex70"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex70.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle f_{\bf w}\left(U_{\text{stacked}}\right)_{0:T,j}=\sum\limits_{i=1}^{n}a_{i}\boldsymbol{W}^{V*}\cdot\left(\frac{1}{N}\sum_{p=1}^{N}\mathbf{1}_{\left(U_{i}\right)_{0p}=1},\cdots,\frac{1}{N}\sum_{p=1}^{N}\mathbf{1}_{\left(U_{i}\right)_{Tp}=1}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝐰</mi></msub><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mtext>stacked</mtext></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><msup><mi>𝑾</mi><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0.222em">∗</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle f_{\bf w}\left(U_{\text{stacked}}\right)_{0:T,j}=\sum\limits_{i=1}^{n}a_{i}\boldsymbol{W}^{V*}\cdot\left(\frac{1}{N}\sum_{p=1}^{N}\mathbf{1}_{\left(U_{i}\right)_{0p}=1},\cdots,\frac{1}{N}\sum_{p=1}^{N}\mathbf{1}_{\left(U_{i}\right)_{Tp}=1}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex71"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex71.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\quad+a_{n+1}\boldsymbol{W}^{V*}\left(\frac{1}{N}\sum\limits_{p=1}^{N}\boldsymbol{1}_{\left({\widetilde{U}}_{\text{q}}\right)_{0p}=1},\cdots,\frac{1}{N}\sum\limits_{p=1}^{N}\boldsymbol{1}_{\left({\widetilde{U}}_{\text{q}}\right)_{T+K+1,p}=1}\right)^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mi>𝑾</mi><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0.222em">∗</mo></mrow></msup><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>U</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mtext>q</mtext></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>U</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mtext>q</mtext></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad+a_{n+1}\boldsymbol{W}^{V*}\left(\frac{1}{N}\sum\limits_{p=1}^{N}\boldsymbol{1}_{\left({\widetilde{U}}_{\text{q}}\right)_{0p}=1},\cdots,\frac{1}{N}\sum\limits_{p=1}^{N}\boldsymbol{1}_{\left({\widetilde{U}}_{\text{q}}\right)_{T+K+1,p}=1}\right)^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex72"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex72.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum\limits_{i=1}^{n}a_{i}\cdot\boldsymbol{W}^{V*}\cdot\left(0,\frac{1-p_{m}}{T}+p_{m},\frac{1-p_{m}}{T},\cdots,\frac{1-p_{m}}{T}\right)^{\top}+a_{n+1}\cdot\boldsymbol{W}^{V*}\cdot\left(p_{m},\frac{1-p_{m}}{T},\cdots,\frac{1-p_{m}}{T}\right)^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>𝑾</mi><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0.222em">∗</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>𝑾</mi><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0.222em">∗</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum\limits_{i=1}^{n}a_{i}\cdot\boldsymbol{W}^{V*}\cdot\left(0,\frac{1-p_{m}}{T}+p_{m},\frac{1-p_{m}}{T},\cdots,\frac{1-p_{m}}{T}\right)^{\top}+a_{n+1}\cdot\boldsymbol{W}^{V*}\cdot\left(p_{m},\frac{1-p_{m}}{T},\cdots,\frac{1-p_{m}}{T}\right)^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E19.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum\limits_{j=1}^{n}a_{j}\cdot\boldsymbol{W}^{V*}\cdot\left(0,\frac{1-p_{m}}{T}+p_{m},\frac{1-p_{m}}{T},\cdots,\frac{1-p_{m}}{T}\right)^{\top}+a_{n+1}\cdot\boldsymbol{W}^{V*}\cdot\left(p_{m},\frac{1-p_{m}}{T},\cdots,\frac{1-p_{m}}{T}\right)^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>𝑾</mi><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0.222em">∗</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>𝑾</mi><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0.222em">∗</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum\limits_{j=1}^{n}a_{j}\cdot\boldsymbol{W}^{V*}\cdot\left(0,\frac{1-p_{m}}{T}+p_{m},\frac{1-p_{m}}{T},\cdots,\frac{1-p_{m}}{T}\right)^{\top}+a_{n+1}\cdot\boldsymbol{W}^{V*}\cdot\left(p_{m},\frac{1-p_{m}}{T},\cdots,\frac{1-p_{m}}{T}\right)^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(19)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p5.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p5.3.1" class="ltx_text">Now consider each entry in (<a href="#A3.E19" title="In Proof. ‣ Appendix C Proof of Claim ‣ A Framework for Quantifying How Pre-Training and Context Benefit In-Context Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">19</span></a>).</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">For simplicity, we assume <math id="A3.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t^{*}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t^{*}=1</annotation></semantics></math>. Then with the optimal <math id="A3.p6.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\boldsymbol{W}^{V*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝑾</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0.222em">∗</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{W}^{V*}</annotation></semantics></math> in (<a href="#A3.E15" title="In Proof. ‣ Appendix C Proof of Claim ‣ A Framework for Quantifying How Pre-Training and Context Benefit In-Context Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15</span></a>) and (<a href="#A3.E16" title="In Proof. ‣ Appendix C Proof of Claim ‣ A Framework for Quantifying How Pre-Training and Context Benefit In-Context Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">16</span></a>), we can derive:</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx60" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex73"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex73.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\quad\sum_{i=1}^{n}a_{i}\cdot\boldsymbol{W}^{V*}\cdot\left(0,\frac{1-p_{m}}{T}+p_{m},\frac{1-p_{m}}{T},\cdots,\frac{1-p_{m}}{T}\right)^{\top}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>𝑾</mi><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0.222em">∗</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad\sum_{i=1}^{n}a_{i}\cdot\boldsymbol{W}^{V*}\cdot\left(0,\frac{1-p_{m}}{T}+p_{m},\frac{1-p_{m}}{T},\cdots,\frac{1-p_{m}}{T}\right)^{\top}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex74"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex74.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{i=1}^{n}a_{i}\cdot\left(\frac{-u^{*}\left(1-p_{m}\right)}{p_{m}}\times 0+(u^{*}+\frac{1}{1-p_{m}})\times\left(\frac{1-p_{m}}{T}+p_{m}\right)+(T-1)\cdot u^{*}\times\frac{1-p_{m}}{T}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{i=1}^{n}a_{i}\cdot\left(\frac{-u^{*}\left(1-p_{m}\right)}{p_{m}}\times 0+(u^{*}+\frac{1}{1-p_{m}})\times\left(\frac{1-p_{m}}{T}+p_{m}\right)+(T-1)\cdot u^{*}\times\frac{1-p_{m}}{T}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E20"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{i=1}^{n}a_{i}\cdot\left(u^{*}+\frac{p_{m}}{1-p_{m}}+\frac{1}{T}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{i=1}^{n}a_{i}\cdot\left(u^{*}+\frac{p_{m}}{1-p_{m}}+\frac{1}{T}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(20)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text">For <math id="A3.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2\leqslant l\leqslant T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>⩽</mo><mi>l</mi><mo>⩽</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2\leqslant l\leqslant T</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx61" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex75"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex75.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\quad\sum_{i=1}^{n}a_{i}\cdot\boldsymbol{W}^{V*}\cdot\left(0,\frac{1-p_{m}}{T}+p_{m},\frac{1-p_{m}}{T},\cdots,\frac{1-p_{m}}{T}\right)^{\top}_{l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>𝑾</mi><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0.222em">∗</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad\sum_{i=1}^{n}a_{i}\cdot\boldsymbol{W}^{V*}\cdot\left(0,\frac{1-p_{m}}{T}+p_{m},\frac{1-p_{m}}{T},\cdots,\frac{1-p_{m}}{T}\right)^{\top}_{l}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex76"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex76.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{i=1}^{n}a_{i}\cdot\left(\frac{-u^{*}\left(1-p_{m}\right)}{p_{m}}\times 0+\left(u^{*}+\frac{1}{1-p_{m}}\right)\times\frac{1-p_{m}}{T}+u^{*}\times\left(\frac{1-p_{m}}{T}+p_{m}\right)+(T-2)\cdot u^{*}\times\frac{1-p_{m}}{T}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{i=1}^{n}a_{i}\cdot\left(\frac{-u^{*}\left(1-p_{m}\right)}{p_{m}}\times 0+\left(u^{*}+\frac{1}{1-p_{m}}\right)\times\frac{1-p_{m}}{T}+u^{*}\times\left(\frac{1-p_{m}}{T}+p_{m}\right)+(T-2)\cdot u^{*}\times\frac{1-p_{m}}{T}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex77"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex77.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{i=1}^{n}a_{i}\cdot\left(u^{*}\times\frac{1-p_{m}}{T}+\frac{1}{T}+u^{*}\times\frac{1-p_{m}}{T}+u^{*}p_{m}+(T-2)\cdot u^{*}\times\frac{1-p_{m}}{T}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{i=1}^{n}a_{i}\cdot\left(u^{*}\times\frac{1-p_{m}}{T}+\frac{1}{T}+u^{*}\times\frac{1-p_{m}}{T}+u^{*}p_{m}+(T-2)\cdot u^{*}\times\frac{1-p_{m}}{T}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{i=1}^{n}a_{i}\cdot\left(\frac{1}{T}+u^{*}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{i=1}^{n}a_{i}\cdot\left(\frac{1}{T}+u^{*}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(21)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p6.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p6.3.1" class="ltx_text">Plug (<a href="#A3.E20" title="In Proof. ‣ Appendix C Proof of Claim ‣ A Framework for Quantifying How Pre-Training and Context Benefit In-Context Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">20</span></a>) and (<a href="#A3.E21" title="In Proof. ‣ Appendix C Proof of Claim ‣ A Framework for Quantifying How Pre-Training and Context Benefit In-Context Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">21</span></a>) to (<a href="#A3.E19" title="In Proof. ‣ Appendix C Proof of Claim ‣ A Framework for Quantifying How Pre-Training and Context Benefit In-Context Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">19</span></a>), we can derive:</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx62" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex78"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex78.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\quad f_{\bf w}\left(U_{\text{stacked}}\right)_{0:T,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝐰</mi></msub><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mtext>stacked</mtext></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad f_{\bf w}\left(U_{\text{stacked}}\right)_{0:T,j}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex79"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex79.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{i=1}^{n}a_{i}\cdot\boldsymbol{W}^{V_{*}}\cdot\left(0,\frac{1-p_{m}}{T}+p_{m},\frac{1-p_{m}}{T},\cdots,\frac{1-p_{m}}{T}\right)^{\top}+a_{n+1}\cdot\boldsymbol{W}^{V_{*}}\cdot\left(p_{m},\frac{1-p_{m}}{T},\cdots,\frac{1-p_{m}}{T}\right)^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>𝑾</mi><msub><mi>V</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>𝑾</mi><msub><mi>V</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{i=1}^{n}a_{i}\cdot\boldsymbol{W}^{V_{*}}\cdot\left(0,\frac{1-p_{m}}{T}+p_{m},\frac{1-p_{m}}{T},\cdots,\frac{1-p_{m}}{T}\right)^{\top}+a_{n+1}\cdot\boldsymbol{W}^{V_{*}}\cdot\left(p_{m},\frac{1-p_{m}}{T},\cdots,\frac{1-p_{m}}{T}\right)^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex80"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex80.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{i=1}^{n}a_{i}\cdot\left(0,u^{*}+\frac{p_{m}}{1-p_{m}}+\frac{1}{T},\frac{1}{{T}}+u^{*},\cdots,\frac{1}{T}+u^{*}\right)^{\top}+a_{n+1}\left(0,\frac{1}{T},\cdots,\frac{1}{T}\right)^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{i=1}^{n}a_{i}\cdot\left(0,u^{*}+\frac{p_{m}}{1-p_{m}}+\frac{1}{T},\frac{1}{{T}}+u^{*},\cdots,\frac{1}{T}+u^{*}\right)^{\top}+a_{n+1}\left(0,\frac{1}{T},\cdots,\frac{1}{T}\right)^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E22"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\left(0,\sum_{i=1}^{n}a_{i}\cdot u^{*}+\frac{p_{m}}{1-p_{m}}+\frac{1}{T},\sum_{i=1}^{n}a_{i}\cdot u^{*}+\frac{1}{T},\cdots,\sum_{i=1}^{n}a_{i}\cdot u^{*}+\frac{1}{T}\right)^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\left(0,\sum_{i=1}^{n}a_{i}\cdot u^{*}+\frac{p_{m}}{1-p_{m}}+\frac{1}{T},\sum_{i=1}^{n}a_{i}\cdot u^{*}+\frac{1}{T},\cdots,\sum_{i=1}^{n}a_{i}\cdot u^{*}+\frac{1}{T}\right)^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(22)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p6.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p6.4.1" class="ltx_text">From the expression in (<a href="#A3.E22" title="In Proof. ‣ Appendix C Proof of Claim ‣ A Framework for Quantifying How Pre-Training and Context Benefit In-Context Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">22</span></a>), we know the largest entry in the vector <math id="A3.p6.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="f_{\bf w}\left(U_{\text{stacked}}\right)_{0:T,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝐰</mi></msub><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mtext>stacked</mtext></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\bf w}\left(U_{\text{stacked}}\right)_{0:T,j}</annotation></semantics></math> corresponds to <math id="A3.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k^{*}_{\text{q}}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>k</mi><mtext>q</mtext><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k^{*}_{\text{q}}=1</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">Now we consider the class labels.</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx63" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex81"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex81.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle f_{\bf w}\left(U_{\text{stacked}}\right)_{T+1:T+K+1,j}=\sum\limits_{i=1}^{n}a_{i}\boldsymbol{W}^{V*}\cdot\left(\frac{1}{N}\sum_{p=1}^{N}(U_{i})_{T+1,p},\cdots,\frac{1}{N}\sum_{p=1}^{N}(U_{i})_{T+K+1,p}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝐰</mi></msub><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mtext>stacked</mtext></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><msup><mi>𝑾</mi><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0.222em">∗</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle f_{\bf w}\left(U_{\text{stacked}}\right)_{T+1:T+K+1,j}=\sum\limits_{i=1}^{n}a_{i}\boldsymbol{W}^{V*}\cdot\left(\frac{1}{N}\sum_{p=1}^{N}(U_{i})_{T+1,p},\cdots,\frac{1}{N}\sum_{p=1}^{N}(U_{i})_{T+K+1,p}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex82"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex82.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\quad+a_{n+1}\boldsymbol{W}^{V*}\left(\frac{1}{N}\sum\limits_{p=1}^{N}{\left({\widetilde{U}}_{\text{q}}\right)_{T+1,p}},\cdots,\frac{1}{N}\sum\limits_{p=1}^{N}\left({\widetilde{U}}_{\text{q}}\right)_{T+K+1,p}\right)^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mi>𝑾</mi><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0.222em">∗</mo></mrow></msup><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>U</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mtext>q</mtext></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>U</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mtext>q</mtext></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad+a_{n+1}\boldsymbol{W}^{V*}\left(\frac{1}{N}\sum\limits_{p=1}^{N}{\left({\widetilde{U}}_{\text{q}}\right)_{T+1,p}},\cdots,\frac{1}{N}\sum\limits_{p=1}^{N}\left({\widetilde{U}}_{\text{q}}\right)_{T+K+1,p}\right)^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex83"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex83.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum\limits_{i=1}^{n}a_{i}\boldsymbol{W}^{V*}\cdot\left(0,Q\cdot\boldsymbol{1}_{k^{*}(U_{i})=1}+\frac{1-Q}{K-1}\cdot\boldsymbol{1}_{k^{*}(U_{i})\neq 1},\frac{1-Q}{K-1},\cdots,\frac{1-Q}{K-1}\cdot\boldsymbol{1}_{k^{*}(U_{i})\neq 1},\frac{1-Q}{K-1}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><msup><mi>𝑾</mi><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0.222em">∗</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum\limits_{i=1}^{n}a_{i}\boldsymbol{W}^{V*}\cdot\left(0,Q\cdot\boldsymbol{1}_{k^{*}(U_{i})=1}+\frac{1-Q}{K-1}\cdot\boldsymbol{1}_{k^{*}(U_{i})\neq 1},\frac{1-Q}{K-1},\cdots,\frac{1-Q}{K-1}\cdot\boldsymbol{1}_{k^{*}(U_{i})\neq 1},\frac{1-Q}{K-1}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex84"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex84.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\quad+a_{n+1}\cdot\left(p_{m},Q(1-p_{m}),\frac{1-Q}{K-1}(1-p_{m}),\cdots,\frac{1-Q}{K-1}(1-p_{m})\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad+a_{n+1}\cdot\left(p_{m},Q(1-p_{m}),\frac{1-Q}{K-1}(1-p_{m}),\cdots,\frac{1-Q}{K-1}(1-p_{m})\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p7.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p7.2.1" class="ltx_text">So <math id="A3.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\forall l=T+2,\cdots,T+K+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\forall l=T+2,\cdots,T+K+1</annotation></semantics></math>, denote <math id="A3.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda_{k}:=\left\{i:k^{*}\left(U_{i}\right)=1\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda_{k}:=\left\{i:k^{*}\left(U_{i}\right)=1\right\}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A3.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k^{*}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k^{*}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> is the class of first token in a sequence.</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx64" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex85"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex85.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle Q\cdot\sum\limits_{i\in\Lambda_{1}}a_{i}+\frac{1-Q}{K-1}\sum\limits_{i\notin\Lambda_{1}}a_{i}\cdot+Q(1-p_{m})\cdot a_{n+1}:=b_{T+2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∉</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em">+</mo><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>:=</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle Q\cdot\sum\limits_{i\in\Lambda_{1}}a_{i}+\frac{1-Q}{K-1}\sum\limits_{i\notin\Lambda_{1}}a_{i}\cdot+Q(1-p_{m})\cdot a_{n+1}:=b_{T+2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="A3.EGx65" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex86"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex86.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle Q\cdot\sum\limits_{i\in\Lambda_{l}}a_{i}+\frac{1-Q}{K-1}\sum\limits_{i\notin\Lambda_{l}}a_{i}\cdot+\frac{1-Q}{K-1}(1-p_{m})\cdot a_{n+1}:=b_{l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∉</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em">+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>:=</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle Q\cdot\sum\limits_{i\in\Lambda_{l}}a_{i}+\frac{1-Q}{K-1}\sum\limits_{i\notin\Lambda_{l}}a_{i}\cdot+\frac{1-Q}{K-1}(1-p_{m})\cdot a_{n+1}:=b_{l}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p7.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p7.3.1" class="ltx_text">In this case, we have</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx66" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex87"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex87.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle f_{\bf w}(U_{\text{stacked}})_{T+k+1,j}=-\frac{q^{*}(1-p_{m})}{p_{m}}\cdot b_{T+1}+\left(q^{*}+\frac{1}{1-p_{m}}\right)\cdot b_{k}+q^{*}\cdot\sum\limits_{r\neq k}b_{r}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝐰</mi></msub><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mtext>stacked</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle f_{\bf w}(U_{\text{stacked}})_{T+k+1,j}=-\frac{q^{*}(1-p_{m})}{p_{m}}\cdot b_{T+1}+\left(q^{*}+\frac{1}{1-p_{m}}\right)\cdot b_{k}+q^{*}\cdot\sum\limits_{r\neq k}b_{r}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p7.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p7.4.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="A3.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q^{*}+\frac{1}{1-p_{m}}&gt;q^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q^{*}+\frac{1}{1-p_{m}}&gt;q^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>, suppose <math id="A3.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{T+2}&gt;b_{k},k\neq T+2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≠</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{T+2}&gt;b_{k},k\neq T+2</annotation></semantics></math>, then we have</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex88" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex88.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underset{k}{\arg}\max f_{\bf w}(U_{\text{stacked}})_{T+k+1,j}=1" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munder accentunder="true"><mi>arg</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">𝑘</mo></munder><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝐰</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mtext>stacked</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underset{k}{\arg}\max f_{\bf w}(U_{\text{stacked}})_{T+k+1,j}=1</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p7.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p7.5.1" class="ltx_text">.
In fact, there always exists <math id="A3.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A3.p7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{T+2}&gt;b_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{T+2}&gt;b_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> holds, if we choose large enough <math id="A3.p7.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{n+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{n+1}</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 1</span></span><span id="Thmlemma1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmlemma1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> denote the set of solution in (<a href="#A3.E15" title="In Proof. ‣ Appendix C Proof of Claim ‣ A Framework for Quantifying How Pre-Training and Context Benefit In-Context Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15</span></a>) and (<a href="#A3.E16" title="In Proof. ‣ Appendix C Proof of Claim ‣ A Framework for Quantifying How Pre-Training and Context Benefit In-Context Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">16</span></a>) that <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L(\boldsymbol{W}^{V})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>V</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L(\boldsymbol{W}^{V})</annotation></semantics></math> We have the following conclusion:</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx67" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex89"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex89.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\forall\boldsymbol{W}^{V*}\in\lim_{\lambda\rightarrow 0}\operatorname{argmin}L_{\ell_{2}}\left(\boldsymbol{W}^{V}\right),\text{there is }\boldsymbol{W}^{V*}\in S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><msup><mi>𝑾</mi><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0.222em">∗</mo></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0.1389em">∈</mo><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">lim</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mi>argmin</mi><msub><mi>L</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>𝑾</mi><mi>V</mi></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">there is </mtext><msup><mi>𝑾</mi><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0.222em">∗</mo></mrow></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\forall\boldsymbol{W}^{V*}\in\lim_{\lambda\rightarrow 0}\operatorname{argmin}L_{\ell_{2}}\left(\boldsymbol{W}^{V}\right),\text{there is }\boldsymbol{W}^{V*}\in S</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p8.1" class="ltx_p">The above lemma directly comes from <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib19" title="" class="ltx_ref">Li et al., 2023b</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Experiment Details for Synthetic Data</h2>

<section id="A4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.1 </span>Data Generation</h3>

<div id="A4.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The vocabulary consists of <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="100" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>100</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">100</annotation></semantics></math> words, with <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T=10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T=10</annotation></semantics></math> topics, denoted as topic ‘0’ to ‘9’. Each topic has <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K=10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K=10</annotation></semantics></math> words, denoted as class ‘0’ to ‘9’. The number of training sequences and test sequences are <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10,000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>10,000</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10,000</annotation></semantics></math>, respectively. We also generate another <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10,000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>10,000</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10,000</annotation></semantics></math> samples to be the context sample for each test sample. The sequence length is set to be a random number between <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="100" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>100</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">100</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="150" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>150</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">150</annotation></semantics></math>. For each training sequence, we randomly draw a key topic <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, with probability <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.55" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.55</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.55</annotation></semantics></math>, the word is drawn from topic <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>. The class generation follows from our setting in Section <a href="#S3.SS1" title="3.1 Data Generation and Encoding ‣ 3 A Statistical Model: Pre-trained Transformer Shifts the Output Distribution ‣ A Framework for Quantifying How Pre-Training and Context Benefit In-Context Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a> with the key class probability <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q=0.91" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.91</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q=0.91</annotation></semantics></math>, and other <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="9" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>9</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">9</annotation></semantics></math> classes occur with probability <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1-Q}{K-1}=0.01" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>0.01</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1-Q}{K-1}=0.01</annotation></semantics></math>. Randomly mask out <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="15\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>15</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">15\%</annotation></semantics></math> of the words in each training sequence. For the test sequences, we set <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{1}=0.7*N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>0.7</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{1}=0.7*N</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{2}=0.3*N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>0.3</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{2}=0.3*N</annotation></semantics></math>, the distribution follow Section <a href="#S3.SS1" title="3.1 Data Generation and Encoding ‣ 3 A Statistical Model: Pre-trained Transformer Shifts the Output Distribution ‣ A Framework for Quantifying How Pre-Training and Context Benefit In-Context Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a> of <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{D}_{\text{q}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mtext>q</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{D}_{\text{q}}</annotation></semantics></math>. The context samples follow <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{D}_{\text{q}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mtext>q</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{D}_{\text{q}}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{1}=0.7*N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>0.7</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{1}=0.7*N</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{2}=0.3*N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>0.3</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{2}=0.3*N</annotation></semantics></math>. Eech test and context sample pair share the same key topic <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> in Section <a href="#S3.SS1" title="3.1 Data Generation and Encoding ‣ 3 A Statistical Model: Pre-trained Transformer Shifts the Output Distribution ‣ A Framework for Quantifying How Pre-Training and Context Benefit In-Context Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a>. Build the prompt by stacking the test and context sequence pair.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.2 </span>Training Hyper parameters</h3>

<div id="A4.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Our experiment set up follows from <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib19" title="" class="ltx_ref">Li et al., 2023b</a>]</cite>. We use a one hidden-layer Bert with one attention head and hidden dimension <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D=104" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>104</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D=104</annotation></semantics></math>. Use Adam optimizer with learning rate <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.01" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.01</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.01</annotation></semantics></math>. The batch size is set to be <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="40" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>40</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">40</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.3 </span>Compare Uniform Attention and Non-Uniform Attention</h3>

<figure id="A4.F6" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2"><img src="2510.22594v1/../figure/train_true.png" id="A4.F6.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_figure_panel ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:215/113;" width="215" height="113" alt="Refer to caption"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2"><img src="2510.22594v1/../figure/dev_true.png" id="A4.F6.g2" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_figure_panel ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:215/113;" width="215" height="113" alt="Refer to caption"></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A4.F6.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 6</span>: </span><span id="A4.F6.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">The training loss and dev loss when the network is trained with uniform attention, i.e, <math id="A4.F6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{W}^{Q}=\boldsymbol{W}^{K}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝑾</mi><mi>Q</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>𝑾</mi><mi>K</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{W}^{Q}=\boldsymbol{W}^{K}=0</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A4.F7" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2"><img src="2510.22594v1/../figure/train_false.png" id="A4.F7.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_figure_panel ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:215/113;" width="215" height="113" alt="Refer to caption"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2"><img src="2510.22594v1/../figure/dev_false.png" id="A4.F7.g2" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_figure_panel ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:215/113;" width="215" height="113" alt="Refer to caption"></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A4.F7.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 7</span>: </span><span id="A4.F7.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">The training loss and dev loss when the network is trained with <math id="A4.F7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{W}^{Q},\boldsymbol{W}^{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝑾</mi><mi>Q</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝑾</mi><mi>K</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{W}^{Q},\boldsymbol{W}^{K}</annotation></semantics></math> updated.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A4.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We conclude from Fig. <a href="#A4.F6" title="Figure 6 ‣ D.3 Compare Uniform Attention and Non-Uniform Attention ‣ Appendix D Experiment Details for Synthetic Data ‣ A Framework for Quantifying How Pre-Training and Context Benefit In-Context Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a> and <a href="#A4.F7" title="Figure 7 ‣ D.3 Compare Uniform Attention and Non-Uniform Attention ‣ Appendix D Experiment Details for Synthetic Data ‣ A Framework for Quantifying How Pre-Training and Context Benefit In-Context Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a> that, freezing the attention to be uniform in the synthetic experiment setting does not influence the training or test performance. Thus, we justify that it is acceptable when we freeze the attention head in our analysis.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A5" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix E </span>Experiment Details for GPT-2 Models</h2>

<div id="A5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Details of concept token training:</span> To train for the concept token for each fine-tuning task/dataset, we add <math id="A5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N=5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N=5</annotation></semantics></math> concept tokens into the input layer of the GPT-2 model, essentially extending the total number of tokens by <math id="A5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N=5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N=5</annotation></semantics></math>. Then we fine-tune on each task/dataset, with only the embedding layer of the GPT-2 model trainable to minimize the prediction error. This will result in <math id="A5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N=5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N=5</annotation></semantics></math> new token embeddings that could represent the concept of the task/dataset. The detailed process is illustrated by the ICL framework in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib22" title="" class="ltx_ref">Min et al. [2022]</a></cite>. The trained GPT-2 model is discarded in the further experiment steps, while the concept token and its corresponding embedding vector (called representation vector in the main text) are kept for further experiment steps
<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A5.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Hyperparameters:</span> We use seven different concept datasets to fine-tune the modified GPT-2 large embedding layer. The model is saved after 10,000 training steps. All seven concept tokens are passed through the embedding layer, getting 7 * 5 * 1280 matrix, number of task * tokens for each task * embedding length, to represent seven concepts. We use the t-SNE <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib28" title="" class="ltx_ref">Van der Maaten and Hinton, 2008</a>]</cite> method to reduce the dimension to 7 * 5 * 2 with perplexity <math id="A5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p=5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p=5</annotation></semantics></math>, and calculate the distance of each concept. After selecting concepts that are similar or dissimilar to the target task based on distance, we use the datasets corresponding to these two sets of concepts to fine-tune the entire model. In test, we use <math id="A5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=16" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>16</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=16</annotation></semantics></math> number of demonstrations for our experiment. We organize the target datasets into batches, with each batch comprising 8 samples grouped together, and run the test with seed 100.
The code we use for in-context inference is based on <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib22" title="" class="ltx_ref">Min et al., 2022</a>]</cite>.
<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A5.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Concept Token Visualization: </span> After we use t-SNE to reduce the dimension to 5 * 2 for each concept, we use the first column as the x-coordinate and the second column as y-coordinate to print five points as in Figure <a href="#S5.F4" title="Figure 4 ‣ 5.1 Experiment settings ‣ 5 Experiment ‣ A Framework for Quantifying How Pre-Training and Context Benefit In-Context Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>. The five concepts corresponding to the same task are printed in the same color.</p>
</div>
