<section id="A6" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix F </span>Comparison of Predictions from Different Prompts </h2>

<div id="A6.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(a) Prediction from (<a href="#S2.E2" title="In 2.2 Modeling ICL prediction with pre-trained LM ‣ 2 The Proposed Framework of Modeling Data Generation and Prediction ‣ A Framework for Quantifying How Pre-Training and Context Benefit In-Context Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>):</span> Set <math id="A6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{Z}=\mathbf{Z}_{\text{stacked}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mtext>stacked</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{Z}=\mathbf{Z}_{\text{stacked}}</annotation></semantics></math> in (<a href="#S2.E5" title="In 2.3 Comparing proposed context construction with existing works ‣ 2 The Proposed Framework of Modeling Data Generation and Prediction ‣ A Framework for Quantifying How Pre-Training and Context Benefit In-Context Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>). In this case, <math id="A6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L=D,G=2n+2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L=D,G=2n+2</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
<table id="A6.EGx68" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.EGx68.1"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.EGx68.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\widehat{y}_{\text{q}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mtext>q</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\widehat{y}_{\text{q}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.EGx68.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=f_{\bf w}(\mathbf{Z})_{1:D,2n+2}=\left(\boldsymbol{W}^{V}X_{1},\boldsymbol{W}^{V}y_{1},\boldsymbol{W}^{V}X_{2},\boldsymbol{W}^{V}y_{2},\cdots,W^{V}X_{\text{q}},\mathbf{0}\right)\cdot\sigma\left(\begin{array}[]{c}X_{1}^{\top}\cdot B\cdot\mathbf{0}\\
y_{1}^{\top}\cdot B\cdot\mathbf{0}\\
\cdots\\
X_{\text{q}}^{\top}\cdot B\cdot\mathbf{0}\\
\mathbf{0}^{\top}\cdot B\cdot\mathbf{0}\end{array}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝐰</mi></msub><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>𝑾</mi><mi>V</mi></msup><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝑾</mi><mi>V</mi></msup><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝑾</mi><mi>V</mi></msup><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝑾</mi><mi>V</mi></msup><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>W</mi><mi>V</mi></msup><msub><mi>X</mi><mtext>q</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><mn>𝟎</mn><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn>𝟎</mn></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn>𝟎</mn></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mo>⋯</mo></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mtext>q</mtext><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn>𝟎</mn></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><msup><mn>𝟎</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn>𝟎</mn></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=f_{\bf w}(\mathbf{Z})_{1:D,2n+2}=\left(\boldsymbol{W}^{V}X_{1},\boldsymbol{W}^{V}y_{1},\boldsymbol{W}^{V}X_{2},\boldsymbol{W}^{V}y_{2},\cdots,W^{V}X_{\text{q}},\mathbf{0}\right)\cdot\sigma\left(\begin{array}[]{c}X_{1}^{\top}\cdot B\cdot\mathbf{0}\\
y_{1}^{\top}\cdot B\cdot\mathbf{0}\\
\cdots\\
X_{\text{q}}^{\top}\cdot B\cdot\mathbf{0}\\
\mathbf{0}^{\top}\cdot B\cdot\mathbf{0}\end{array}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.E28"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{2n+2}\sum\limits_{i=1}^{n}W^{V}(X_{i}+y_{i})+\frac{1}{2n+2}W^{V}{X}_{\text{q}}^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>W</mi><mi>V</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>W</mi><mi>V</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mtext>q</mtext><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{2n+2}\sum\limits_{i=1}^{n}W^{V}(X_{i}+y_{i})+\frac{1}{2n+2}W^{V}{X}_{\text{q}}^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(28)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(b) Prediction from (<a href="#S2.EGx3" title="2.3 Comparing proposed context construction with existing works ‣ 2 The Proposed Framework of Modeling Data Generation and Prediction ‣ A Framework for Quantifying How Pre-Training and Context Benefit In-Context Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.3</span></a>):</span> Set <math id="A6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{Z}=\mathbf{Z}_{\text{stacked}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mtext>stacked</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{Z}=\mathbf{Z}_{\text{stacked}}</annotation></semantics></math> in (<a href="#S2.E5" title="In 2.3 Comparing proposed context construction with existing works ‣ 2 The Proposed Framework of Modeling Data Generation and Prediction ‣ A Framework for Quantifying How Pre-Training and Context Benefit In-Context Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>). In this case, <math id="A6.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L=2D,G=n+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L=2D,G=n+1</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
<table id="A6.EGx69" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.EGx69.1"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.EGx69.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\widehat{y}_{\text{q}}=f_{\bf w}(\boldsymbol{Z})_{D+1:2D,n+1}=\left(\boldsymbol{W}^{V^{\prime}}\boldsymbol{Z}\right)\cdot\mathcal{M}\cdot\sigma\left(\frac{\left(\boldsymbol{W}^{K^{\prime}}\boldsymbol{Z}\right)^{\top}\left(\boldsymbol{W}^{Q^{\prime}}\boldsymbol{Z}\right)}{\sqrt{2D}}\right),\;\mathcal{M}:=\left(\begin{array}[]{cc}I_{n}&amp;0\\
0&amp;0\end{array}\right)\in\mathbb{R}^{(n+1)\times(n+1)}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mtext>q</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝐰</mi></msub><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒁</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>𝑾</mi><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msup><mi>𝒁</mi><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝑾</mi><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒁</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝑾</mi><msup><mi>Q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒁</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\widehat{y}_{\text{q}}=f_{\bf w}(\boldsymbol{Z})_{D+1:2D,n+1}=\left(\boldsymbol{W}^{V^{\prime}}\boldsymbol{Z}\right)\cdot\mathcal{M}\cdot\sigma\left(\frac{\left(\boldsymbol{W}^{K^{\prime}}\boldsymbol{Z}\right)^{\top}\left(\boldsymbol{W}^{Q^{\prime}}\boldsymbol{Z}\right)}{\sqrt{2D}}\right),\;\mathcal{M}:=\left(\begin{array}[]{cc}I_{n}&amp;0\\
0&amp;0\end{array}\right)\in\mathbb{R}^{(n+1)\times(n+1)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.p1.3" class="ltx_p">More specifically, in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib36" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhang et al., 2023a</a>]</cite>, the weight has following structure:</p>
<table id="A6.EGx70" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.EGx70.1"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.EGx70.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\boldsymbol{W}^{V^{\prime}}=\left[\begin{array}[]{cc}\mathbf{0}_{D\times D}&amp;\mathbf{0}_{D\times D}\\
\mathbf{0}_{D\times D}&amp;I_{D}\end{array}\right]\in\mathbb{R}^{2D\times 2D},\quad{\boldsymbol{W}^{K^{\prime}}}^{\top}{\boldsymbol{W}^{Q^{\prime}}}=\left[\begin{array}[]{cc}B^{\prime}&amp;\mathbf{0}_{D\times D}\\
\mathbf{0}_{D\times D}&amp;\mathbf{0}_{D\times D}\end{array}\right]\quad\text{ where }B^{\prime}\in\mathbb{R}^{D\times D}\text{. }" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝑾</mi><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mn>𝟎</mn><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mn>𝟎</mn><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mn>𝟎</mn><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>D</mi></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mmultiscripts><mi>𝑾</mi><mrow></mrow><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></mmultiscripts><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑾</mi><msup><mi>Q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msup><mi>B</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mtd><mtd><msub><mn>𝟎</mn><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mn>𝟎</mn><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mn>𝟎</mn><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mtext> where </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>.</mtext></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\boldsymbol{W}^{V^{\prime}}=\left[\begin{array}[]{cc}\mathbf{0}_{D\times D}&amp;\mathbf{0}_{D\times D}\\
\mathbf{0}_{D\times D}&amp;I_{D}\end{array}\right]\in\mathbb{R}^{2D\times 2D},\quad{\boldsymbol{W}^{K^{\prime}}}^{\top}{\boldsymbol{W}^{Q^{\prime}}}=\left[\begin{array}[]{cc}B^{\prime}&amp;\mathbf{0}_{D\times D}\\
\mathbf{0}_{D\times D}&amp;\mathbf{0}_{D\times D}\end{array}\right]\quad\text{ where }B^{\prime}\in\mathbb{R}^{D\times D}\text{. }</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.p1.4" class="ltx_p">Thus, we can derive</p>
<table id="A6.EGx71" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.EGx71.1"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.EGx71.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\widehat{y}_{\text{q}}=\left(y_{1},y_{2},\cdots,y_{n},\mathbf{0}\right)\cdot\sigma\left(\begin{array}[]{ll}X_{1}^{\top}\cdot B^{\prime}\cdot X_{\text{q}}\\
X_{2}^{\top}\cdot B^{\prime}\cdot X_{\text{q}}\\
\quad\quad\cdots\\
X_{n}^{\top}\cdot B^{\prime}\cdot X_{\text{q}}\end{array}\right)=\sum\limits_{i=1}^{n}\sigma_{i}y_{i}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mtext>q</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mn>𝟎</mn><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mtext>q</mtext></msub></mrow></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mtext>q</mtext></msub></mrow></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mo>⋯</mo></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>n</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mtext>q</mtext></msub></mrow></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\widehat{y}_{\text{q}}=\left(y_{1},y_{2},\cdots,y_{n},\mathbf{0}\right)\cdot\sigma\left(\begin{array}[]{ll}X_{1}^{\top}\cdot B^{\prime}\cdot X_{\text{q}}\\
X_{2}^{\top}\cdot B^{\prime}\cdot X_{\text{q}}\\
\quad\quad\cdots\\
X_{n}^{\top}\cdot B^{\prime}\cdot X_{\text{q}}\end{array}\right)=\sum\limits_{i=1}^{n}\sigma_{i}y_{i},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.p1.5" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A6.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum\limits_{i=1}^{n}\sigma_{i}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum\limits_{i=1}^{n}\sigma_{i}=1</annotation></semantics></math>, and each <math id="A6.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{i}=\frac{\exp\left(X_{i}^{\top}\cdot B^{\prime}\cdot X_{\text{q}}\right)}{\sum\limits_{l=1}^{n}\exp\left(X_{l}^{\top}\cdot B^{\prime}\cdot X_{\text{q}}\right)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mtext>q</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><munderover><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" movablelimits="false" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>l</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mtext>q</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{i}=\frac{\exp\left(X_{i}^{\top}\cdot B^{\prime}\cdot X_{\text{q}}\right)}{\sum\limits_{l=1}^{n}\exp\left(X_{l}^{\top}\cdot B^{\prime}\cdot X_{\text{q}}\right)}</annotation></semantics></math> .</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A7" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix G </span>Limitation and Future Work</h2>

<div id="A7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In our work, we requires each class within a topic only includes one word. We make this assumption to simplify our analysis. However, in more realistic setting, one class can contain multiple words, which requires a more complicated modeling. Further, we assume uniform attention in our network, which can be extended to more realistic setting where <math id="A7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W^{Q},W^{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>W</mi><mi>Q</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>W</mi><mi>K</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W^{Q},W^{K}</annotation></semantics></math> are updated. These extension will left to future work.</p>
</div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
</article>
</div>
</div>
